-- allium: 3
-- actions.allium — Forgejo Actions: GitHub-Actions-compatible CI/CD driven by workflow files in the repository.
--
-- Scope: everything between "something happened in a repository" and "a runner
--   reported a result": workflow discovery and event matching, workflow runs,
--   jobs and their dependency graph, tasks handed to runners, runner
--   registration and the runner protocol, logs, step summaries, job outputs,
--   artifacts, secrets, variables, the automatic token and OIDC ID tokens,
--   scheduled (cron) workflows, manual dispatch, pull-request approval for
--   untrusted contributors, concurrency groups, cancellation, re-runs, run
--   priority, commit-status reporting, and every background clean-up job.
-- Includes: Workflow, WorkflowRun, Job, Task, TaskStep, TaskOutput, Runner,
--   RunnerRegistrationToken, ActionsScope, Secret, Variable, Artifact,
--   Schedule, ScheduleSpec, TrustedContributor.
-- Excludes:
--   - ActionsCache: Forgejo hosts no cache server; the runner hosts the
--     actions/cache backend. Forgejo only grants a write-everything cache
--     scope inside the runtime token (see Task.runtime_token_cache_scope).
--   - Workflow YAML semantics (expressions, matrix expansion, step execution,
--     container handling): executed by the runner and the shared jobparser
--     library; referenced here through black-box functions (job_definitions,
--     evaluate_if, expand_incomplete_job, matching_workflows).
--   - The legacy v1-v3 artifact upload protocol's chunk/file layout (several
--     rows per artifact): a compatibility concern; artifacts are modelled as
--     one logical (run, name) object, as the v4 protocol stores them.
--   - Pre-translated pre-execution error strings stored by Forgejo v13 and the
--     legacy OIDC subject format `legacy_forgejo_15`: data-import concerns
--     (an open question keeps the subject format choice visible).
--   - `GITEA_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN`/`gitea_runtime_token` aliases: kept only as
--     names the runner expects; the rebuild exposes one automatic token under
--     whatever names its runner protocol requires.
--   - The `repository` hook event (repository created/migrated, fork created)
--     reaching workflows: it has no GitHub workflow equivalent and a new
--     repository is empty; not specified.
--   - Tasks-version polling counter (lets idle runners skip a query): a
--     performance optimisation; behaviourally a runner may poll at any time.
--   - Doctor fixes for runners whose owner/repository vanished: replaced by
--     the deletion reactions below.
--   - Rendering of logs/summary markdown, badge SVG drawing: presentation.
--
-- Emits:
--   WorkflowRunAttemptStarted(run)                     -- a run was created or re-run
--   WorkflowRunStatusChanged(run, prior_status)        -- non-final status change
--   WorkflowRunCompleted(run, prior_status)            -- run reached a final status
--   WorkflowJobAttemptStarted(job)                     -- a job was created or re-run
--   WorkflowJobStatusChanged(job, prior_status)        -- non-final job status change
--   WorkflowJobCompleted(job, prior_status)            -- job reached a final status;
--       -- notifications mails the trigger user on failure when run.notify_email
--   code/CommitStatusReported(repository, commit_sha, context, state, target_url, description, creator)
--       -- emitted on code's behalf with creator = the Actions bot; code records the CommitStatus
--   IdTokenIssued(task, audience, expires_at)
--
-- Reacts to:
--   code/PushReceived(push)                     -- push; also refreshes schedules on default branch
--   code/RefCreated(repository, pusher, ref_kind, ref_name, commit_sha)  -- create
--   code/RefDeleted(repository, pusher, ref_kind, ref_name)              -- delete
--   repositories/MirrorSyncPushed(repository, ref_name, commits)          -- push (pull-mirror sync, doer: owner)
--   repositories/MirrorRefCreated(repository, ref_name)                   -- create (pull-mirror sync, doer: owner)
--   repositories/MirrorRefDeleted(repository, ref_name)                   -- delete (pull-mirror sync, doer: owner)
--   code/DefaultBranchChanged(repository, old_name, new_name, by)        -- re-detect schedules
--   code/BranchRenamed(repository, from_name, to_name, by)               -- re-detect schedules
--   repositories/RepositoryForked(source, fork, doer)       -- fork (on the source)
--   repositories/RepositoryArchived(repository, doer)       -- drop schedules, cancel scheduled runs
--   repositories/RepositoryUnarchived(repository, doer)     -- re-detect schedules
--   repositories/RepoUnitDisabled(repository, kind)         -- actions unit off: drop schedules
--   repositories/RepoUnitEnabled(repository, kind)          -- actions unit on: re-detect schedules
--   repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)        -- remove all actions data
--   accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, purge, delete_contributions),
--   organizations/OrganizationDeleted(organization)         -- remove owner-scoped data
--   accounts/UserBlocked(blocker, blocked)                  -- revoke the blocked user's trust
--   issues/IssueOpened(issue, mentions), issues/IssueTitleChanged(issue, doer, old_title),
--   issues/IssueContentChanged(issue, doer, old_content),
--   issues/IssueClosed(issue, doer, comment), issues/IssueReopened(issue, doer, comment),
--   issues/IssueAssigneeChanged(issue, doer, assignee, removed, comment),
--   issues/IssueMilestoneChanged(issue, doer, old_milestone),
--   issues/IssueLabelsChanged(issue, doer, added, removed), issues/IssueLabelsCleared(issue, doer)
--   issues/IssueCommentCreated(issue, comment, doer, mentions),
--   issues/IssueCommentEdited(comment, doer, old_content), issues/IssueCommentDeleted(comment, doer)
--   pulls/PullRequestOpened(pull_request), pulls/PullRequestSynchronized(pull_request, doer),
--   pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger), pulls/ReviewSubmitted(review),
--   pulls/ReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, reviewer),
--   pulls/ReviewRequestRemoved(pull_request, doer, reviewer),
--   pulls/PullRequestTargetBranchChanged(pull_request, doer, old_base_branch)
--   releases/ReleasePublished(release), releases/ReleaseUpdated(release, doer),
--   releases/ReleaseDeleted(release, doer)
--   packages/PackageVersionCreated(version, publisher), packages/PackageVersionDeleted(version, doer)
--   wiki/WikiPageCreated(repository, doer, page), wiki/WikiPageEdited(repository, doer, page),
--   wiki/WikiPageDeleted(repository, doer, page)
--   administration scheduled tasks (cron "run now" and the timer alike):
--   ZombieActionsTaskStopDue(), EndlessActionsTaskStopDue(),
--   AbandonedActionsJobCancellationDue(), LingeringActionsLogTransferDue(),
--   ActionsScheduleStartDue(), ActionsCleanupDue(), ActionsUserCleanupDue(),
--   OfflineRunnerCleanupDue(older_than, global_scope_only). Each sweep emits the
--   same per-item internal trigger as the matching temporal rule, so the work
--   is described once, in the rule that consumes that trigger.

use "./accounts.allium" as accounts
use "./organizations.allium" as organizations
use "./repositories.allium" as repositories
use "./access.allium" as access
use "./code.allium" as code
use "./issues.allium" as issues
use "./pulls.allium" as pulls
use "./releases.allium" as releases
use "./packages.allium" as packages
use "./wiki.allium" as wiki
use "./quota.allium" as quota
use "./administration.allium" as administration

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- One `workflow_dispatch` input declared by a workflow.
-- from: services/actions/workflows.go:50
value DispatchInput {
    key: String
    description: String?
    required: Boolean
    default_value: String?
    input_type: String            -- string | boolean | choice | number | environment
}

-- What the workflow parser produces for one job of a run before it is stored.
-- A matrix job or a reusable-workflow call expands into several definitions.
-- from: services/actions/job.go:153
value JobDefinition {
    key: String                   -- the `jobs.<key>` identifier
    namespace: String             -- non-empty for jobs expanded from a reusable workflow
    name: String
    needs: Set<String>
    runs_on: Set<String>
    is_incomplete: Boolean        -- matrix / runs-on / with depend on outputs of needed jobs
    if_statically_false: Boolean  -- `if:` evaluated server-side to false
    is_workflow_call_outer: Boolean  -- caller of a reusable workflow; its work is in child jobs
    oidc_requested: Boolean       -- `enable-openid-connect: true`
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The protocol a runner speaks to fetch work and report back.
-- from: routers/api/actions/runner/runner.go:40
contract RunnerProtocol {
    register: (registration_token: String, name: String, labels: Set<String>, version: String, ephemeral: Boolean) -> Runner
    declare: (labels: Set<String>, version: String) -> Runner
    fetch_task: (capacity: Integer, request_key: String?) -> Set<Task>
    update_task: (task: Task, result: ActionStatus?, outputs: Set<TaskOutput>) -> Task
    update_log: (task: Task, from_index: Integer, row_count: Integer, no_more: Boolean) -> Integer

    @invariant AuthenticatedByRunnerToken
        -- Every call except register carries the runner's identity and its
        -- runner token; a wrong token is indistinguishable from an unknown runner.
        -- Every authenticated call refreshes the runner's last_online_at;
        -- update_task and update_log also refresh last_active_at.

    @invariant RequestKeyIdempotence
        -- A fetch that carries a request key returns, on retry with the same
        -- key from the same runner, exactly the tasks assigned under that key
        -- (with freshly minted task tokens) instead of assigning new ones.
        -- Concurrent fetches with one key are refused until the first ends.

    @invariant LogAppendOnly
        -- update_log appends rows from the acknowledged index; rows already
        -- acknowledged are ignored and the response carries the new
        -- acknowledged index. After no_more the log is archived and further
        -- rows are refused.

    @invariant OutputsWriteOnce
        -- An output key is recorded once per task; later values for the same
        -- key are ignored. Keys over 255 characters and values over 1 MiB are
        -- dropped. The response lists the keys already stored.
}

-- The workflow parser the rebuild must supply (GitHub Actions YAML dialect).
-- from: services/actions/notifier_helper.go:423
contract WorkflowParser {
    job_definitions: (repository: repositories/Repository, workflow_file: String, commit_sha: String) -> Set<JobDefinition>
    matching_workflows: (repository: repositories/Repository, event: TriggeringEvent, activity: String, ref: String, commit_sha: String) -> Set<Workflow>

    @invariant ExpressionContext
        -- Expressions see the git context (repository, ref, sha, event
        -- payload, actor, run number/attempt), `vars`, dispatch `inputs`,
        -- and — once needed jobs are done — `needs.<id>.outputs/result`.
        -- `secrets` are never available to server-side evaluation.

    @invariant ReusableWorkflowsArePublicOrLocal
        -- `uses:` of a reusable workflow resolves a path in the same commit,
        -- or `owner/repo/path@ref` on the same instance when owner and
        -- repository are public; anything else is left to the runner.
}

-- The artifact upload/download protocol used from inside a running job.
-- from: routers/api/actions/artifactsv4.go:1
contract ArtifactProtocol {
    create_artifact: (name: String, expires_at: Timestamp?) -> Artifact
    upload_content: (artifact: Artifact, bytes: Integer) -> Artifact
    finalize_artifact: (artifact: Artifact, size: Integer) -> Artifact
    list_artifacts: (name_filter: String?) -> Set<Artifact>
    download_url: (artifact: Artifact) -> String

    @invariant ScopedToRun
        -- A task only sees and writes artifacts of its own run, and only
        -- while the task is running.

    @invariant SignedTransferUrls
        -- Upload and download URLs are signed, bound to the task and the
        -- artifact, and expire; the transfer requests themselves carry no
        -- other credentials.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Status shared by runs, jobs, tasks and steps.
-- from: models/actions/status.go:17
enum ActionStatus { waiting | blocked | running | success | failure | cancelled | skipped }

-- The repository event that may start workflows (the webhook event kinds
-- Actions understands; see webhooks/HookEventKind).
-- from: modules/actions/github.go:30
enum TriggeringEvent {
    push | create | delete | fork
    | issues | issue_assign | issue_label | issue_milestone
    | issue_comment | pull_request_comment
    | pull_request | pull_request_sync | pull_request_assign | pull_request_label
    | pull_request_milestone | pull_request_review_request
    | pull_request_review_approved | pull_request_review_rejected | pull_request_review_comment
    | release | package | wiki | schedule | workflow_dispatch
}

-- Event names a workflow lists under `on:`.
-- from: modules/actions/github.go:12
enum WorkflowEvent {
    push | create | delete | fork | issues | issue_comment
    | pull_request | pull_request_target | pull_request_review | pull_request_review_comment
    | release | registry_package | gollum | schedule | workflow_dispatch | workflow_call
}

-- How a run behaves relative to other runs in its concurrency group.
-- from: models/actions/run.go:31
enum ConcurrencyMode { unlimited | queue_behind | cancel_in_progress }

-- Where runners, secrets, variables and registration tokens live.
-- from: models/actions/runner.go:25
enum ScopeKind { instance | user | organization | repository }

-- from: models/actions/artifact.go:22
enum ArtifactStatus { upload_pending | upload_confirmed | expired | pending_deletion | deleted }

-- Why a run failed before any job could execute.
-- from: models/actions/pre_execution_errors.go:21
enum PreExecutionError {
    event_detection_error | job_parsing_error
    | incomplete_matrix_missing_job | incomplete_matrix_missing_output | incomplete_matrix_unknown_cause
    | incomplete_runs_on_missing_job | incomplete_runs_on_missing_output
    | incomplete_runs_on_missing_matrix_dimension | incomplete_runs_on_unknown_cause
    | incomplete_with_missing_job | incomplete_with_missing_output
    | incomplete_with_missing_matrix_dimension | incomplete_with_unknown_cause
    | unknown_job_in_needs
}

-- from: modules/setting/actions.go:72
enum LogCompression { none | zstd }


------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The owner of runners, secrets, variables and registration tokens: the
-- whole instance, one user, one organization or one repository. Exactly one
-- of owner_user / owner_org / repository is set unless kind = instance.
-- from: models/actions/runner.go:25
entity ActionsScope {
    kind: ScopeKind
    owner_user: accounts/User?
    owner_org: organizations/Organization?
    repository: repositories/Repository?

    runners: Runner with scope = this
    secrets: Secret with scope = this
    variables: Variable with scope = this
    registration_tokens: RunnerRegistrationToken with scope = this

    active_registration_tokens: registration_tokens where is_active = true

    invariant ExactlyOneOwner {
        (kind = instance implies owner_user = null and owner_org = null and repository = null)
        and (kind = user implies owner_user != null and owner_org = null and repository = null)
        and (kind = organization implies owner_org != null and owner_user = null and repository = null)
        and (kind = repository implies repository != null and owner_user = null and owner_org = null)
    }
}

-- A workflow file found in one of the workflow directories of a repository.
-- Only the first existing directory of .forgejo/workflows, .gitea/workflows,
-- .github/workflows is used; files ending .yml or .yaml (recursively) count.
-- The disabled flag is per repository and per file name.
-- from: modules/actions/workflows.go:59
entity Workflow {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    file_name: String             -- e.g. build.yml; identifies the workflow
    directory: String             -- e.g. .forgejo/workflows
    name: String?                 -- `name:`; defaults to the path
    events: Set<WorkflowEvent>
    has_dispatch_trigger: Boolean -- `workflow_dispatch` is among the events
    has_schedule_trigger: Boolean -- `schedule` is among the events
    dispatch_inputs: Set<DispatchInput>
    is_disabled: Boolean

    path: directory + "/" + file_name
}

-- One execution of one workflow file for one event. Its status is the
-- aggregate of its jobs' statuses.
-- from: models/actions/run.go:44
entity WorkflowRun {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    index: Integer                -- per-repository run number, starts at 1
    title: String                 -- `run-name:` or first line of the commit message; max 255
    workflow_file: String
    workflow_directory: String
    trigger_user: accounts/User   -- the Actions bot for scheduled runs
    event: TriggeringEvent
    trigger_event: WorkflowEvent  -- the `on:` entry that matched
    activity: String?             -- e.g. opened, synchronize, labeled
    ref: String
    commit_sha: String
    workflow_source_sha: String?  -- base-branch commit for pull_request_target
    schedule: Schedule?
    inputs: Set<String>           -- dispatch inputs as key=value
    status: ActionStatus
    created_at: Timestamp
    started_at: Timestamp?
    stopped_at: Timestamp?
    previous_attempts_duration: Duration
    attempt: Integer
    notify_email: Boolean         -- workflow `enable-email-notifications: true`

    -- pull request trust
    pull_request: pulls/PullRequest?
    pull_request_poster: accounts/User?
    is_fork_pull_request: Boolean
    needs_approval: Boolean
    approved_by: accounts/User?

    concurrency_group: String     -- case-insensitive
    concurrency_mode: ConcurrencyMode

    pre_execution_error: PreExecutionError?
    pre_execution_error_details: String?
    has_permissions_warning: Boolean   -- a job declares `permissions:` which is not honoured

    priority: Integer             -- -128..127; higher is dispatched first
    prioritized: Boolean          -- a user asked for this run to go first
    jobs_expanded: Boolean        -- the job graph has been materialised

    jobs: Job with run = this
    artifacts: Artifact with run = this

    pending_jobs: jobs where status in {waiting, blocked, running}

    is_valid: pre_execution_error = null
    is_done: status in {success, failure, cancelled, skipped}
    can_be_rerun: is_valid and is_done
    is_scheduled: trigger_event = schedule
    is_dispatched: trigger_event = workflow_dispatch
    secrets_withheld: is_fork_pull_request and trigger_event != pull_request_target

    aggregated_status:
        if jobs.count > 0 and jobs.all(j => j.status = skipped): skipped
        else if jobs.count > 0 and jobs.all(j => j.status in {success, skipped}): success
        else if jobs.any(j => j.status = running): running
        else if jobs.any(j => j.status = waiting): waiting
        else if jobs.any(j => j.status = blocked): blocked
        else if jobs.any(j => j.status = cancelled): cancelled
        else: failure
    status_is_stale: aggregated_status != status
    awaiting_job_expansion: not jobs_expanded and pre_execution_error = null
    awaiting_failure_record: not jobs_expanded and pre_execution_error != null

    invariant PriorityRange { priority >= -128 and priority <= 127 }
}

-- One job of a run (one entry under `jobs:`, or one matrix combination, or
-- one job of an expanded reusable workflow).
-- from: models/actions/run_job.go:46
entity Job {
    run: WorkflowRun
    key: String
    namespace: String
    name: String                  -- max 255
    needs: Set<String>
    runs_on: Set<String>          -- labels a runner must all carry
    status: ActionStatus
    attempt: Integer              -- starts at 1, incremented by each re-run
    handle: String                -- identifies this attempt; a runner may ask for it explicitly
    started_at: Timestamp?
    stopped_at: Timestamp?
    status_changed_at: Timestamp
    is_incomplete: Boolean
    is_workflow_call_outer: Boolean
    oidc_requested: Boolean
    is_assigned: Boolean          -- a task exists for the current attempt

    tasks: Task with job = this

    needs_done: needs.count = 0 or all_needed_jobs_done(this)
    needs_succeeded: needs.count = 0 or all_needed_jobs_succeeded_or_skipped(this)
    all_needs_skipped: needs.count > 0 and all_needed_jobs_skipped(this)
    is_done: status in {success, failure, cancelled, skipped}
    ready_to_unblock: status = blocked and needs_done and not run.needs_approval

    transitions status {
        waiting -> running
        waiting -> cancelled
        waiting -> failure
        blocked -> waiting
        blocked -> skipped
        blocked -> success
        blocked -> failure
        blocked -> cancelled
        running -> success
        running -> failure
        running -> cancelled
        running -> skipped
        success -> waiting
        success -> blocked
        failure -> waiting
        failure -> blocked
        cancelled -> waiting
        cancelled -> blocked
        skipped -> waiting
        skipped -> blocked
    }
}

-- One attempt of a job handed to one runner. Its token is the job's
-- automatic token (FORGEJO_TOKEN), valid only while the task runs.
-- from: models/actions/task.go:22
entity Task {
    job: Job
    runner: Runner
    attempt: Integer
    status: ActionStatus
    started_at: Timestamp
    stopped_at: Timestamp?
    last_activity_at: Timestamp
    token: String                 -- secret; only the hash is kept
    request_key: String?
    is_fork_pull_request: Boolean
    oidc_enabled: Boolean

    -- logs
    log_length: Integer           -- lines
    log_size: Integer             -- bytes
    log_archived: Boolean         -- moved from the live buffer to (compressed) storage
    log_expired: Boolean          -- removed after the retention period

    steps: TaskStep with task = this
    outputs: TaskOutput with task = this

    is_stopped: stopped_at != null
    token_is_usable: status = running
    token_repository_access: if is_fork_pull_request: "read" else: "write"
    runtime_token_cache_scope: "write"
}

-- One step of a task, as listed in the job definition.
-- from: models/actions/task_step.go:14
entity TaskStep {
    task: Task
    index: Integer
    name: String                  -- max 255
    status: ActionStatus
    started_at: Timestamp?
    stopped_at: Timestamp?
    log_index: Integer
    log_length: Integer
    summary: String?              -- GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY markdown, at most 1 MiB
}

-- A job output reported by the runner (`jobs.<id>.outputs`).
-- from: models/actions/task_output.go:16
entity TaskOutput {
    task: Task
    key: String                   -- at most 255 characters
    value: String                 -- at most 1 MiB
}

-- A machine that executes jobs. It belongs to a scope and can only pick jobs
-- of repositories inside that scope.
-- from: models/actions/runner.go:36
entity Runner {
    scope: ActionsScope
    name: String                  -- max 255, need not be unique
    description: String?
    version: String?
    labels: Set<String>
    is_ephemeral: Boolean         -- deleted after its single task completes
    token: String                 -- secret; only the hash is kept
    created_at: Timestamp
    last_online_at: Timestamp?
    last_active_at: Timestamp?
    has_taken_task: Boolean       -- ever been assigned a task
    is_busy: Boolean              -- currently has a running task

    tasks: Task with runner = this

    health:
        if last_online_at = null: offline
        else if last_online_at + config.runner_offline_after <= now: offline
        else if last_active_at = null: idle
        else if last_active_at + config.runner_idle_after <= now: idle
        else: active
    is_online: health in {active, idle}
    has_used_its_single_task: is_ephemeral and has_taken_task

    serves(repo): scope.kind = instance
        or (scope.kind = repository and scope.repository = repo)
        or (scope.kind = user and repo.owner_user = scope.owner_user)
        or (scope.kind = organization and repo.owner_org = scope.owner_org)
}

-- A shared secret runners present to register themselves into a scope.
-- Creating a new one invalidates the previous ones of the same scope; it can
-- be used any number of times while active.
-- from: models/actions/runner_token.go:27
entity RunnerRegistrationToken {
    scope: ActionsScope
    token: String
    is_active: Boolean
    created_at: Timestamp
}

-- An encrypted value made available to jobs as `secrets.NAME`. Never shown
-- again after it is set. Instance-wide secrets do not exist.
-- from: models/secret/secret.go:37
entity Secret {
    scope: ActionsScope
    name: String                  -- stored upper-case
    value: String                 -- write-only; encrypted at rest
    created_at: Timestamp

    invariant NotInstanceWide { scope.kind != instance }
}

-- A plain configuration value made available to jobs as `vars.NAME`.
-- from: models/actions/variable.go:29
entity Variable {
    scope: ActionsScope
    name: String                  -- stored upper-case
    value: String
    created_at: Timestamp
    updated_at: Timestamp?
}

-- A named bundle of files uploaded by a job, downloadable until it expires.
-- from: models/actions/artifact.go:35
entity Artifact {
    run: WorkflowRun
    name: String
    uploaded_by: Task
    size: Integer                 -- bytes as uploaded
    compressed_size: Integer      -- bytes stored (counts towards the owner's artifacts quota)
    status: ArtifactStatus
    created_at: Timestamp
    expires_at: Timestamp

    is_downloadable: status = upload_confirmed
    is_listed: status in {upload_confirmed, expired}

    transitions status {
        upload_pending -> upload_confirmed
        upload_pending -> pending_deletion
        upload_confirmed -> expired
        upload_confirmed -> pending_deletion
        expired -> pending_deletion
        pending_deletion -> deleted
        terminal: deleted
    }
}

-- A scheduled workflow registered from the default branch's head commit.
-- All schedules of a repository are replaced whenever the default branch moves.
-- from: models/actions/schedule.go:19
entity Schedule {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    workflow_file: String
    workflow_directory: String
    title: String
    ref: String
    commit_sha: String
    created_at: Timestamp

    specs: ScheduleSpec with schedule = this
}

-- One `cron:` entry of a scheduled workflow.
-- from: models/actions/schedule_spec.go:20
entity ScheduleSpec {
    schedule: Schedule
    cron: String                  -- 5-field cron or @descriptor; may start with TZ= / CRON_TZ=
    time_zone: String?            -- `timezone:`; UTC when absent
    next_run_at: Timestamp
    previous_run_at: Timestamp?
}

-- A pull-request poster a maintainer chose to always trust in a repository,
-- so their fork pull requests run without approval.
-- from: models/actions/user.go:17
entity TrustedContributor {
    user: accounts/User
    repository: repositories/Repository
    trusted_with_pull_requests: Boolean
    last_access_at: Timestamp
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [actions] ENABLED
    actions_enabled: Boolean = true
    -- [actions] LOG_RETENTION_DAYS (values <= 0 mean the default)
    log_retention: Duration = 365.days
    -- [actions] LOG_COMPRESSION
    log_compression: LogCompression = zstd
    -- [actions] ARTIFACT_RETENTION_DAYS (values <= 0 mean the default)
    artifact_retention: Duration = 90.days
    -- [actions] DEFAULT_ACTIONS_URL: base for `uses:` without a host
    default_actions_url: String = "https://data.forgejo.org"
    -- [actions] ZOMBIE_TASK_TIMEOUT: running task without any update
    zombie_task_timeout: Duration = 10.minutes
    -- [actions] ENDLESS_TASK_TIMEOUT: running task that never ends
    endless_task_timeout: Duration = 3.hours
    -- [actions] ABANDONED_JOB_TIMEOUT: waiting/blocked job no runner picked
    abandoned_job_timeout: Duration = 24.hours
    -- [actions] SKIP_WORKFLOW_STRINGS: in commit message or PR title, suppresses runs
    skip_workflow_strings: Set<String> = {"[skip ci]", "[ci skip]", "[no ci]", "[skip actions]", "[actions skip]"}
    -- [actions] LIMIT_DISPATCH_INPUTS
    limit_dispatch_inputs: Integer = 100
    -- [actions] CONCURRENCY_GROUP_QUEUE_ENABLED: false lets queue_behind runs run in parallel
    concurrency_group_queue_enabled: Boolean = true
    -- [actions] ID_TOKEN_EXPIRATION_TIME (seconds)
    id_token_lifetime: Duration = 1.hour

    -- fixed behaviour (not configurable in Forgejo)
    runner_offline_after: Duration = 1.minute
    runner_idle_after: Duration = 10.seconds
    runtime_token_lifetime: Duration = 24.hours
    trusted_contributor_expiry: Duration = 90.days
    max_title_length: Integer = 255
    max_name_length: Integer = 255
    max_output_key_length: Integer = 255
    max_output_value_bytes: Integer = 1048576
    max_step_summary_bytes: Integer = 1048576
    max_log_line_bytes: Integer = 65536
    lingering_log_age: Duration = 24.hours

    -- [cron.*] background jobs (owned by administration/CronTask; schedules here)
    stop_zombie_tasks_interval: Duration = 5.minutes
    stop_endless_tasks_interval: Duration = 30.minutes
    cancel_abandoned_jobs_interval: Duration = 6.hours
    start_schedule_tasks_interval: Duration = 1.minute
    -- [cron.cleanup_offline_runners] ENABLED / OLDER_THAN / GLOBAL_SCOPE_ONLY
    offline_runner_cleanup_enabled: Boolean = false
    offline_runner_cleanup_age: Duration = 24.hours
    offline_runner_cleanup_global_only: Boolean = true
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: event intake (other modules' triggers become workflow events)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Each pushed branch or tag is a `push` event on its new head.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:560
rule PushStartsWorkflows {
    when: code/PushReceived(push)
    ensures:
        for update in push.ref_updates where new_sha != null and ref_kind in {branch_ref, tag_ref}:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: push.repository, doer: push.pusher, event: push, activity: null, ref: full_ref_name(update), commit_sha: update.new_sha, pull_request: null)
            if update.ref_kind = branch_ref and update.ref_name = push.repository.default_branch:
                SchedulesNeedRefresh(repository: push.repository)
    @guidance
        -- Pushes by the Actions bot never start workflows (see
        -- DetectWorkflowRuns) but still refresh schedules, because a
        -- scheduled job may itself push to the default branch.
        -- Pull-mirror syncs are handled by MirrorSyncStartsWorkflows.
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:610
rule RefCreationStartsWorkflows {
    when: code/RefCreated(repository, pusher, ref_kind, ref_name, commit_sha)
    requires: ref_kind in {branch_ref, tag_ref}
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository, doer: pusher, event: create, activity: null, ref: qualified_ref(ref_kind, ref_name), commit_sha, pull_request: null)
}

-- `delete` runs workflows from the default branch.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:628
rule RefDeletionStartsWorkflows {
    when: code/RefDeleted(repository, pusher, ref_kind, ref_name)
    requires: ref_kind in {branch_ref, tag_ref}
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository, doer: pusher, event: delete, activity: null, ref: qualified_ref(ref_kind, ref_name), commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- Pull-mirror syncs start the same push / create / delete workflows as user
-- pushes, with the repository owner as doer. A synced ref is a full ref name.
-- mirror_pusher(repository): the owning user or organisation account
-- (repositories/mirror_pusher); head_commit_sha(commits): the sync's head
-- commit, pinned so a concurrent push cannot substitute a newer commit;
-- ref_head_sha(repository, ref_name): the commit the ref now points to.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:645
-- from: services/mirror/mirror_pull.go:600
rule MirrorSyncStartsWorkflows {
    when: repositories/MirrorSyncPushed(repository, ref_name, commits)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: repository, doer: mirror_pusher(repository), event: push, activity: null, ref: ref_name, commit_sha: head_commit_sha(commits), pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:681
rule MirrorRefCreationStartsWorkflows {
    when: repositories/MirrorRefCreated(repository, ref_name)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: repository, doer: mirror_pusher(repository), event: create, activity: null, ref: ref_name, commit_sha: ref_head_sha(repository, ref_name), pull_request: null)
}

-- `delete` runs workflows from the default branch.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:686
rule MirrorRefDeletionStartsWorkflows {
    when: repositories/MirrorRefDeleted(repository, ref_name)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: repository, doer: mirror_pusher(repository), event: delete, activity: null, ref: ref_name, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- `fork` fires on the source repository and runs from its default branch.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:410
rule ForkStartsWorkflows {
    when: repositories/RepositoryForked(source, fork, doer)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: source, doer, event: fork, activity: null, ref: "refs/heads/" + source.default_branch, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- Issue events run from the default branch. Pull requests are opened by pulls.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:41
rule IssueOpenedStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueOpened(issue, mentions)
    requires: not issue.is_pull
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer: issue.poster, event: issues, activity: "opened", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- Title edits: `edited` on issues, or on pull_request for a PR.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:62
rule IssueTitleChangeStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueTitleChanged(issue, doer, old_title)
    ensures: IssueEditedForActions(issue, editor: doer)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:69
rule IssueContentChangeStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueContentChanged(issue, doer, old_content)
    ensures: IssueEditedForActions(issue, editor: doer)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:75
rule IssueEditedStartsWorkflows {
    when: IssueEditedForActions(issue, editor)
    ensures:
        if issue.is_pull:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer: editor, event: pull_request, activity: "edited", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: issue.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer: editor, event: issues, activity: "edited", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:114
rule IssueClosedStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueClosed(issue, doer, comment)
    ensures:
        if issue.is_pull:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: pull_request, activity: "closed", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: issue.pull_request)
            PullRequestClosedForActions(pull_request: issue.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: issues, activity: "closed", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:114
rule IssueReopenedStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueReopened(issue, doer, comment)
    ensures:
        if issue.is_pull:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: pull_request, activity: "reopened", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: issue.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: issues, activity: "reopened", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:169
rule AssigneeChangeStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueAssigneeChanged(issue, doer, assignee, removed, comment)
    let activity = if removed: "unassigned" else: "assigned"
    ensures:
        if issue.is_pull:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: pull_request_assign, activity, ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: issue.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: issue_assign, activity, ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:188
rule MilestoneChangeStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueMilestoneChanged(issue, doer, old_milestone)
    let activity = if issue.milestone = null: "demilestoned" else: "milestoned"
    ensures:
        if issue.is_pull:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: pull_request_milestone, activity, ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: issue.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: issue_milestone, activity, ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- Label changes match activity types `labeled` / `unlabeled`.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:206
rule LabelChangeStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueLabelsChanged(issue, doer, added, removed)
    let activity = if added.count > 0: "labeled" else: "unlabeled"
    ensures:
        if issue.is_pull:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: pull_request_label, activity, ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: issue.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: issue_label, activity, ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:206
rule LabelsClearedStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueLabelsCleared(issue, doer)
    ensures:
        if issue.is_pull:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: pull_request_label, activity: "unlabeled", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: issue.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: issue_label, activity: "unlabeled", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- Comments match `issue_comment` (types created/edited/deleted) on issues
-- and pull requests alike; they run from the default branch.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:275
rule CommentCreatedStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueCommentCreated(issue, comment, doer, mentions)
    ensures:
        if issue.is_pull:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: pull_request_comment, activity: "created", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: issue.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: issue.repository, doer, event: issue_comment, activity: "created", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:287
rule CommentEditedStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueCommentEdited(comment, doer, old_content)
    ensures:
        if comment.issue.is_pull:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: comment.issue.repository, doer, event: pull_request_comment, activity: "edited", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: comment.issue.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: comment.issue.repository, doer, event: issue_comment, activity: "edited", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:302
rule CommentDeletedStartsWorkflows {
    when: issues/IssueCommentDeleted(comment, doer)
    ensures:
        if comment.issue.is_pull:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: comment.issue.repository, doer, event: pull_request_comment, activity: "deleted", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: comment.issue.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: comment.issue.repository, doer, event: issue_comment, activity: "deleted", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- The pull request's head commit at the time of the event is used, never a
-- later one rediscovered asynchronously.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:365
rule PullRequestOpenedStartsWorkflows {
    when: pulls/PullRequestOpened(pull_request)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: pull_request.base_repository, doer: pull_request.issue.poster, event: pull_request, activity: "opened",
        ref: pull_ref(pull_request), commit_sha: pull_request.head_commit_sha, pull_request)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:725
rule PullRequestSynchronizedStartsWorkflows {
    when: pulls/PullRequestSynchronized(pull_request, doer)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: pull_request.base_repository, doer, event: pull_request_sync, activity: "synchronize",
        ref: pull_ref(pull_request), commit_sha: pull_request.head_commit_sha, pull_request)
}

-- A merge is a `closed` pull_request event on the merge commit.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:519
rule PullRequestMergedStartsWorkflows {
    when: pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: pull_request.base_repository, doer: merger, event: pull_request, activity: "closed",
        ref: merge_commit_of(pull_request), commit_sha: merge_commit_of(pull_request), pull_request)
}

-- Approve / request changes / comment reviews; activity `submitted`/`edited`.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:438
rule ReviewStartsWorkflows {
    when: pulls/ReviewSubmitted(review)
    ensures:
        if review.kind = approve:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: review.pull_request.base_repository, doer: review.reviewer, event: pull_request_review_approved,
                activity: "submitted", ref: review.commit_sha, commit_sha: review.commit_sha, pull_request: review.pull_request)
        else if review.kind = request_changes:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: review.pull_request.base_repository, doer: review.reviewer, event: pull_request_review_rejected,
                activity: "submitted", ref: review.commit_sha, commit_sha: review.commit_sha, pull_request: review.pull_request)
        else:
            ForgeEventObserved(repository: review.pull_request.base_repository, doer: review.reviewer, event: pull_request_review_comment,
                activity: "submitted", ref: review.commit_sha, commit_sha: review.commit_sha, pull_request: review.pull_request)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:486
rule ReviewRequestStartsWorkflows {
    when: pulls/ReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, reviewer)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: pull_request.base_repository, doer: requester, event: pull_request_review_request, activity: "review_requested",
        ref: pull_ref(pull_request), commit_sha: null, pull_request)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:486
rule ReviewRequestRemovalStartsWorkflows {
    when: pulls/ReviewRequestRemoved(pull_request, doer, reviewer)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: pull_request.base_repository, doer, event: pull_request_review_request, activity: "review_request_removed",
        ref: pull_ref(pull_request), commit_sha: null, pull_request)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:754
rule TargetBranchChangeStartsWorkflows {
    when: pulls/PullRequestTargetBranchChanged(pull_request, doer, old_base_branch)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: pull_request.base_repository, doer, event: pull_request, activity: "edited",
        ref: pull_ref(pull_request), commit_sha: null, pull_request)
}

-- Release events run on the release's tag; `updated` matches type `edited`.
-- from: services/actions/notifier_helper.go:520
rule ReleasePublishedStartsWorkflows {
    when: releases/ReleasePublished(release)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: release.repository, doer: release.publisher, event: release, activity: "published",
        ref: "refs/tags/" + release.tag_name, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:696
rule ReleaseUpdatedStartsWorkflows {
    when: releases/ReleaseUpdated(release, doer)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: release.repository, doer, event: release, activity: "edited", ref: "refs/tags/" + release.tag_name, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:701
rule ReleaseDeletedStartsWorkflows {
    when: releases/ReleaseDeleted(release, doer)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: release.repository, doer, event: release, activity: "deleted", ref: "refs/tags/" + release.tag_name, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- `registry_package` (type `published` / `deleted`), only for packages
-- linked to a repository.
-- from: services/actions/notifier_helper.go:540
rule PackagePublishedStartsWorkflows {
    when: packages/PackageVersionCreated(version, publisher)
    requires: version.package.repository != null
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: version.package.repository, doer: publisher, event: package, activity: "published", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:715
rule PackageDeletedStartsWorkflows {
    when: packages/PackageVersionDeleted(version, doer)
    requires: version.package.repository != null
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository: version.package.repository, doer, event: package, activity: "deleted", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- Wiki edits match `gollum` and run from the default branch.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:785
rule WikiCreatedStartsWorkflows {
    when: wiki/WikiPageCreated(repository, doer, page)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository, doer, event: wiki, activity: "created", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:797
rule WikiEditedStartsWorkflows {
    when: wiki/WikiPageEdited(repository, doer, page)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository, doer, event: wiki, activity: "edited", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:809
rule WikiDeletedStartsWorkflows {
    when: wiki/WikiPageDeleted(repository, doer, page)
    ensures: ForgeEventObserved(repository, doer, event: wiki, activity: "deleted", ref: null, commit_sha: null, pull_request: null)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: workflow discovery and run creation
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The heart of event-driven runs. For the event's commit (or the default
-- branch for default-branch events) every workflow whose `on:` matches the
-- event and its filters gets a run.
-- from: services/actions/notifier_helper.go:142
rule DetectWorkflowRuns {
    when: ForgeEventObserved(repository, doer, event, activity, ref, commit_sha, pull_request)
    requires: config.actions_enabled
    requires: actions_unit_enabled(repository)
    requires: not repository.is_empty
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: not is_actions_bot(doer)
    requires: event in {push, pull_request, pull_request_sync}
        implies not skip_marker_present(commit_sha, pull_request, config.skip_workflow_strings)
    requires: event = pull_request_sync
        implies not pull_request_run_exists_for_commit(repository, commit_sha)
    let effective_ref = if runs_from_default_branch(event): "refs/heads/" + repository.default_branch else: ref
    let needs_approval = pull_request != null and not runs_from_default_branch(event)
        and pull_request.is_fork
        and not is_trusted_contributor(pull_request.issue.poster, repository)
        and not is_trusted_contributor(doer, repository)
    ensures:
        for workflow in matching_workflows(repository, event, activity, effective_ref, commit_sha, pull_request)
                where not is_disabled:
            WorkflowRunRequested(workflow, doer, event, activity, ref: effective_ref, commit_sha, pull_request,
                needs_approval: needs_approval and not is_pull_request_target(workflow, event))
    @guidance
        -- runs_from_default_branch: delete, fork, issues (all kinds),
        -- issue_comment, pull_request_comment, wiki, schedule, workflow_dispatch.
        -- Filters (matching_workflows): push branches/branches-ignore/tags/
        -- tags-ignore/paths/paths-ignore (paths ignored for tags; when both
        -- branch and tag filters exist only one family must match);
        -- pull_request(_target) types (default opened/reopened/synchronize),
        -- branches against the base branch, paths against the merge base;
        -- issues/issue_comment/release/registry_package/pull_request_review
        -- `types` with glob matching and the activity renames
        -- (synchronized->synchronize, label_updated->labeled,
        -- label_cleared->unlabeled, updated->edited, created->published,
        -- reviewed->submitted|edited). A workflow whose `on:` cannot be parsed
        -- still yields a run that fails with event_detection_error.
        -- pull_request_target workflows are read from the base branch head
        -- and never need approval (they run the base branch's code).
        -- When the poster is untrusted but the doer is trusted, a
        -- non-synchronize event reads workflows from the base branch instead
        -- of the (possibly modified) head.
        -- Trust: implicit for a non-fork pull request or a user with write
        -- access to the Actions unit; explicit via TrustedContributor (never
        -- for restricted users).
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier_helper.go:363
rule CreateWorkflowRun {
    when: WorkflowRunRequested(workflow, doer, event, activity, ref, commit_sha, pull_request, needs_approval)
    ensures: WorkflowRun.created(
        repository: workflow.repository,
        index: next_run_index(workflow.repository),
        title: run_title(workflow, commit_sha),
        workflow_file: workflow.file_name,
        workflow_directory: workflow.directory,
        trigger_user: doer,
        event: event,
        trigger_event: workflow_trigger(workflow, event),
        activity: activity,
        ref: ref,
        commit_sha: commit_sha,
        workflow_source_sha: workflow_source_commit(workflow, pull_request),
        schedule: null,
        inputs: {},
        status: waiting,
        created_at: now,
        started_at: null,
        stopped_at: null,
        previous_attempts_duration: 0.seconds,
        attempt: 1,
        notify_email: workflow_notifies_by_email(workflow),
        pull_request: pull_request,
        pull_request_poster: pull_request?.issue.poster,
        is_fork_pull_request: pull_request != null and pull_request.is_fork,
        needs_approval: needs_approval,
        approved_by: null,
        concurrency_group: concurrency_group_for_event(workflow, event, ref),
        concurrency_mode: concurrency_mode_for_event(workflow, event),
        pre_execution_error: workflow_pre_execution_error(workflow, event),
        pre_execution_error_details: null,
        has_permissions_warning: declares_permissions(workflow),
        priority: 0,
        prioritized: false,
        jobs_expanded: false
    )
    @guidance
        -- Concurrency: `concurrency.group` (case-insensitive) and
        -- `cancel-in-progress`. Without a group the default group is
        -- "<ref>_<workflow>_<trigger>__auto". Without cancel-in-progress,
        -- push and pull_request_sync runs cancel in progress, others are
        -- unlimited; cancel-in-progress=false with an explicit group queues
        -- behind; cancel-in-progress=false without a group is unlimited.
        -- The run title is `run-name:` when it evaluates non-empty, else the
        -- first line of the commit message; at most 255 characters.
}

-- A valid run gets its jobs. Jobs with `needs`, with inputs still unknown,
-- or in a run awaiting approval start blocked; a job whose `if:` is false
-- server-side is skipped; the rest wait for a runner.
-- from: services/actions/job.go:153
rule ExpandRunIntoJobs {
    when: run: WorkflowRun.awaiting_job_expansion
    ensures:
        run.jobs_expanded = true
        if run.concurrency_mode = cancel_in_progress:
            ConcurrencyGroupCancellationRequested(run)
        for definition in job_definitions(run.repository, run.workflow_file, run.commit_sha):
            Job.created(
                run: run,
                key: definition.key,
                namespace: definition.namespace,
                name: definition.name,
                needs: definition.needs,
                runs_on: definition.runs_on,
                status: initial_job_status(definition, run.needs_approval),
                attempt: 1,
                handle: new_handle(),
                started_at: null,
                stopped_at: null,
                status_changed_at: now,
                is_incomplete: definition.is_incomplete,
                is_workflow_call_outer: definition.is_workflow_call_outer,
                oidc_requested: definition.oidc_requested,
                is_assigned: false
            )
        WorkflowRunAttemptStarted(run)
        RunConsistencyCheckRequested(run)
    @guidance
        -- initial_job_status: blocked when the definition has needs, is
        -- incomplete, or the run needs approval; else skipped when its `if:`
        -- is statically false; else waiting.
        -- Job definitions come from the workflow at the run's source commit,
        -- with variables, dispatch inputs and git context available to
        -- expressions. Local reusable workflows (`uses: ./.forgejo/...`) and
        -- same-instance reusable workflows (`owner/repo/path@ref`, public
        -- owners and public repositories only) are expanded into namespaced
        -- jobs when the calling job has no `runs-on`. Names are cut at 255.
        -- WorkflowJobAttemptStarted is emitted for each job except incomplete ones.
        -- A new run with cancel-in-progress cancels the rest of its group
        -- (services/actions/notifier_helper.go:440).
}

-- A run that could not be parsed still appears, failed, with one failed job
-- named after the workflow file.
-- from: services/actions/notifier_helper.go:417
rule RecordPreExecutionFailure {
    when: run: WorkflowRun.awaiting_failure_record
    ensures:
        run.jobs_expanded = true
        if run.concurrency_mode = cancel_in_progress:
            ConcurrencyGroupCancellationRequested(run)
        Job.created(
            run: run,
            key: run.workflow_file,
            namespace: "",
            name: run.workflow_file,
            needs: {},
            runs_on: {},
            status: failure,
            attempt: 1,
            handle: new_handle(),
            started_at: null,
            stopped_at: now,
            status_changed_at: now,
            is_incomplete: false,
            is_workflow_call_outer: false,
            oidc_requested: false,
            is_assigned: false
        )
        WorkflowRunAttemptStarted(run)
}

-- Checks that would otherwise leave a job blocked forever fail the run:
-- `needs` naming an unknown job, a matrix depending on a job not in
-- `needs`, `runs-on` naming a matrix dimension that does not exist.
-- from: services/actions/run.go:178
rule CheckRunConsistency {
    when: RunConsistencyCheckRequested(run)
    let problem = consistency_problem(run.repository, run.workflow_file, run.commit_sha)
    requires: problem != null
    ensures: RunFailedBeforeExecution(run, error: problem)
}

-- from: services/actions/run.go:154
rule FailRunBeforeExecution {
    when: RunFailedBeforeExecution(run, error)
    requires: run.pre_execution_error = null
    ensures:
        run.pre_execution_error = error
        RunKillRequested(run, as_failure: true)
}

-- Every other run of the same repository and concurrency group that still
-- has pending jobs is cancelled.
-- from: services/actions/schedule_tasks.go:245
rule CancelOtherRunsInConcurrencyGroup {
    when: ConcurrencyGroupCancellationRequested(run)
    ensures:
        for other in WorkflowRuns where repository = run.repository
                and concurrency_group = run.concurrency_group
                and pending_jobs.count > 0:
            if other != run:
                RunKillRequested(run: other, as_failure: false)
}

-- Stop every unfinished job (and its task) of a run: cancelled, or failed
-- when the run failed before execution.
-- from: services/actions/run.go:85
rule KillRun {
    when: RunKillRequested(run, as_failure)
    ensures:
        for job in run.jobs where status in {waiting, blocked, running}:
            if as_failure:
                job.status = failure
            else:
                job.status = cancelled
            job.stopped_at = now
            job.status_changed_at = now
            WorkflowJobCompleted(job, prior_status: job.status)
            for task in job.tasks where status = running:
                TaskStopRequested(task, as_failure)
        run.needs_approval = false
}

-- from: services/actions/task.go:222
rule StopTask {
    when: TaskStopRequested(task, as_failure)
    requires: task.status = running
    ensures:
        if as_failure:
            task.status = failure
        else:
            task.status = cancelled
        task.stopped_at = now
        task.runner.is_busy = false
        for step in task.steps where status in {waiting, blocked, running}:
            if as_failure:
                step.status = failure
            else:
                step.status = cancelled
            step.stopped_at = now
        if task.runner.is_ephemeral:
            not exists task.runner
}

-- The run's status always follows its jobs.
-- from: models/actions/run.go:313
rule RunStatusFollowsJobs {
    when: run: WorkflowRun.status_is_stale
    let prior = run.status
    ensures:
        run.status = run.aggregated_status
        if run.aggregated_status in {success, failure, cancelled, skipped}:
            run.stopped_at = now
            WorkflowRunCompleted(run, prior_status: prior)
        else:
            WorkflowRunStatusChanged(run, prior_status: prior)
    @guidance
        -- Aggregation: all skipped -> skipped; all success/skipped ->
        -- success; any running -> running; any waiting -> waiting; any
        -- blocked -> blocked; any cancelled -> cancelled; otherwise failure.
        -- A run finishing makes queued runs of its concurrency group eligible.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: job dependency graph
------------------------------------------------------------

-- All needed jobs are done: a regular job becomes waiting, unless its `if:`
-- (default `success()`) is false — then it is skipped.
-- from: services/actions/job_emitter.go:155
rule BlockedJobBecomesWaiting {
    when: job: Job.ready_to_unblock
    requires: not job.is_workflow_call_outer
    requires: not job.is_incomplete
    requires: evaluate_if(job)
    ensures:
        job.status = waiting
        job.status_changed_at = now
        WorkflowJobStatusChanged(job, prior_status: blocked)
}

-- from: services/actions/job_emitter.go:351
rule BlockedJobIsSkipped {
    when: job: Job.ready_to_unblock
    requires: not job.is_workflow_call_outer
    requires: not job.is_incomplete
    requires: not evaluate_if(job)
    ensures:
        job.status = skipped
        job.stopped_at = now
        job.status_changed_at = now
        WorkflowJobCompleted(job, prior_status: blocked)
}

-- A job whose matrix / runs-on / `with:` needed outputs of other jobs is
-- re-parsed once they are done and replaced by the jobs it expands to. If
-- it still cannot be resolved the run fails (or the job is skipped when the
-- missing values come from skipped jobs).
-- from: services/actions/job_emitter.go:257
rule IncompleteJobExpands {
    when: job: Job.ready_to_unblock
    requires: job.is_incomplete
    let outcome = expand_incomplete_job(job)
    ensures:
        if outcome.skipped:
            job.status = skipped
            job.stopped_at = now
            job.status_changed_at = now
            WorkflowJobCompleted(job, prior_status: blocked)
        else if outcome.error != null:
            RunFailedBeforeExecution(run: job.run, error: outcome.error)
        else:
            for definition in outcome.definitions:
                Job.created(
                    run: job.run,
                    key: definition.key,
                    namespace: definition.namespace,
                    name: definition.name,
                    needs: definition.needs,
                    runs_on: definition.runs_on,
                    status: initial_job_status(definition, false),
                    attempt: 1,
                    handle: new_handle(),
                    started_at: null,
                    stopped_at: null,
                    status_changed_at: now,
                    is_incomplete: definition.is_incomplete,
                    is_workflow_call_outer: definition.is_workflow_call_outer,
                    oidc_requested: definition.oidc_requested,
                    is_assigned: false
                )
            not exists job
}

-- A reusable-workflow caller job finishes when its inner jobs do.
-- from: services/actions/job_emitter.go:176
rule WorkflowCallOuterJobFinishes {
    when: job: Job.ready_to_unblock
    requires: job.is_workflow_call_outer
    requires: not job.is_incomplete
    ensures:
        if not job.needs_succeeded:
            job.status = failure
        else if job.all_needs_skipped:
            job.status = skipped
        else:
            job.status = success
        job.stopped_at = now
        job.status_changed_at = now
        WorkflowJobCompleted(job, prior_status: blocked)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: pull-request approval and contributor trust
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Approving releases the run: jobs without `needs` start waiting.
-- from: services/actions/run.go:106
rule ApproveRun {
    when: RunApproved(run, approver)
    requires: run.needs_approval
    ensures:
        for job in run.jobs where status = blocked and needs.count = 0:
            job.status = waiting
            job.status_changed_at = now
            WorkflowJobStatusChanged(job, prior_status: blocked)
        run.needs_approval = false
        run.approved_by = approver
}

-- "Approve once": every run of this pull request awaiting approval.
-- from: services/actions/trust.go:300
rule UserApprovesPullRequestRuns {
    when: UserApprovesPullRequestRunsOnce(user, pull_request)
    requires: may_delegate_actions_trust(user, pull_request.base_repository)
    ensures:
        for run in WorkflowRuns where pull_request = pull_request and needs_approval = true:
            RunApproved(run, approver: user)
}

-- "Always trust": remember the poster and approve all their pending runs.
-- from: services/actions/trust.go:255
rule UserAlwaysTrustsPoster {
    when: UserAlwaysTrustsPullRequestPoster(user, pull_request)
    requires: may_delegate_actions_trust(user, pull_request.base_repository)
    let poster = pull_request.issue.poster
    ensures: TrustedContributor.created(
        user: poster,
        repository: pull_request.base_repository,
        trusted_with_pull_requests: true,
        last_access_at: now
    )
    ensures:
        for run in WorkflowRuns where repository = pull_request.base_repository
                and pull_request_poster = poster and needs_approval = true:
            RunApproved(run, approver: user)
}

-- "Deny": cancel every unfinished run of this pull request.
-- from: services/actions/trust.go:285
rule UserDeniesPullRequestRuns {
    when: UserDeniesPullRequestRuns(user, pull_request)
    requires: may_delegate_actions_trust(user, pull_request.base_repository)
    ensures:
        for run in WorkflowRuns where pull_request = pull_request
                and status in {waiting, blocked, running}:
            RunKillRequested(run, as_failure: false)
}

-- "Revoke": forget the poster and cancel all their unfinished runs.
-- from: services/actions/trust.go:240
rule UserRevokesPosterTrust {
    when: UserRevokesPullRequestPosterTrust(user, pull_request)
    requires: may_delegate_actions_trust(user, pull_request.base_repository)
    let poster = pull_request.issue.poster
    ensures:
        for tc in TrustedContributors where user = poster and repository = pull_request.base_repository:
            not exists tc
        for run in WorkflowRuns where repository = pull_request.base_repository
                and pull_request_poster = poster and status in {waiting, blocked, running}:
            RunKillRequested(run, as_failure: false)
}

-- Closing a pull request cancels runs still waiting for approval.
-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:141
rule ClosedPullRequestCancelsUnapprovedRuns {
    when: PullRequestClosedForActions(pull_request)
    ensures:
        for run in WorkflowRuns where pull_request = pull_request and needs_approval = true:
            RunKillRequested(run, as_failure: false)
}

-- Explicit trust lapses when it has not been relied upon for 90 days.
-- from: models/actions/user.go:91
rule TrustedContributorExpires {
    when: tc: TrustedContributor.last_access_at + config.trusted_contributor_expiry <= now
    ensures: TrustedContributorLapsed(trusted_contributor: tc)
    @guidance
        -- last_access_at is refreshed (at most daily) whenever the trust is
        -- consulted for a pull-request event. Swept weekly by cron
        -- (administration/ActionsUserCleanupDue).
}

-- from: models/actions/user.go:91
rule RevokeLapsedTrust {
    when: TrustedContributorLapsed(trusted_contributor)
    requires: exists trusted_contributor
    ensures: not exists trusted_contributor
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: runners
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A runner registers itself with an active registration token. The token
-- stays usable for further registrations until it is rotated.
-- from: routers/api/actions/runner/runner.go:47
rule RunnerRegisters {
    when: RunnerRegistersWithToken(registration_token, name, labels, version, is_ephemeral)
    requires: registration_token.is_active
    requires: name != ""
    ensures: Runner.created(
        scope: registration_token.scope,
        name: name,
        description: null,
        version: version,
        labels: labels,
        is_ephemeral: is_ephemeral,
        token: new_secret_token(),
        created_at: now,
        last_online_at: null,
        last_active_at: null,
        has_taken_task: false,
        is_busy: false
    )
    @guidance
        -- The name is cut at 255 characters. The response returns the
        -- runner's identity and token exactly once.
        -- An offline registration path (CLI with a shared secret) creates or
        -- updates a runner whose identity derives from that secret.
}

-- An administrator pre-creates a runner and is shown its token once, for
-- the runner to be configured with (no registration token needed).
-- from: routers/web/shared/actions/runners.go:252
rule UserCreatesRunner {
    when: UserCreatesRunnerInScope(user, scope, name, description, is_ephemeral)
    requires: may_manage_actions_scope(user, scope)
    requires: valid_runner_name(name)
    ensures: Runner.created(
        scope: scope,
        name: name,
        description: description,
        version: null,
        labels: {},
        is_ephemeral: is_ephemeral,
        token: new_secret_token(),
        created_at: now,
        last_online_at: null,
        last_active_at: null,
        has_taken_task: false,
        is_busy: false
    )
    @guidance
        -- valid_runner_name: non-empty, at most 255 characters.
}

-- Every authenticated call: the runner announces its labels and version.
-- from: routers/api/actions/runner/runner.go:124
rule RunnerDeclaresCapabilities {
    when: RunnerDeclares(runner, labels, version)
    ensures:
        runner.labels = labels
        runner.version = version
        runner.last_online_at = now
}

-- from: routers/web/shared/actions/runners.go:319
rule UserEditsRunner {
    when: UserEditsRunnerDetails(user, runner, name, description)
    requires: may_manage_actions_scope(user, runner.scope)
    requires: valid_runner_name(name)
    ensures:
        runner.name = name
        runner.description = description
}

-- Rotating the runner token disconnects the runner until it is
-- reconfigured with the new token, shown once.
-- from: routers/web/shared/actions/runners.go:374
rule UserRegeneratesRunnerToken {
    when: UserRegeneratesRunnerSecret(user, runner)
    requires: may_manage_actions_scope(user, runner.scope)
    ensures: runner.token = new_secret_token()
}

-- from: routers/web/shared/actions/runners.go:407
rule UserDeletesRunner {
    when: UserDeletesRunnerFromScope(user, runner)
    requires: may_manage_actions_scope(user, runner.scope)
    ensures: not exists runner
    @guidance
        -- Tasks already assigned to the runner keep running until they time
        -- out as zombies. A deleted runner's identity is never reused.
}

-- Issue a fresh registration token and invalidate the scope's older ones.
-- The runners page and API issue one automatically when none exists.
-- from: models/actions/runner_token.go:60
rule UserResetsRegistrationToken {
    when: UserRequestsNewRegistrationToken(user, scope)
    requires: may_manage_actions_scope(user, scope)
    ensures:
        for old in scope.registration_tokens:
            old.is_active = false
        RunnerRegistrationToken.created(scope: scope, token: new_secret_token(), is_active: true, created_at: now)
}

-- Ephemeral runners that already ran their task are deleted by the daily
-- clean-up even if the immediate deletion was missed.
-- from: services/actions/cleanup.go:155
rule UsedEphemeralRunnerRemoved {
    when: runner: Runner.has_used_its_single_task
    requires: not runner.is_busy
    ensures: RunnerRemovalDue(runner)
}

-- Optional cron: delete runners that have been offline (or never came
-- online) for longer than the configured age; by default instance runners only.
-- from: models/actions/runner.go:426
rule OfflineRunnerRemoved {
    when: runner: Runner.created_at + config.offline_runner_cleanup_age <= now
    requires: config.offline_runner_cleanup_enabled
    requires: runner.last_online_at = null or runner.last_online_at + config.offline_runner_cleanup_age <= now
    requires: config.offline_runner_cleanup_global_only implies runner.scope.kind = instance
    ensures: RunnerRemovalDue(runner)
}

-- One place where a swept runner (used ephemeral or long offline) goes away.
-- from: services/actions/cleanup.go:155
rule RemoveSweptRunner {
    when: RunnerRemovalDue(runner)
    requires: exists runner
    ensures: not exists runner
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: task assignment and runner reports
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A polling runner is given the highest-priority waiting job it can run:
-- the job's repository is within the runner's scope, Actions is enabled
-- there, the runner carries every `runs-on` label, and (with the
-- concurrency queue) no older pending or running run of the same
-- concurrency group blocks it.
-- from: services/actions/task.go:453
rule RunnerFetchesTask {
    when: RunnerFetchesTask(runner, job, request_key)
    requires: job.status = waiting
    requires: not job.is_assigned
    requires: runner.scope.kind = instance
        or (runner.scope.kind = repository and runner.scope.repository = job.run.repository)
        or (runner.scope.kind = user and job.run.repository.owner_user = runner.scope.owner_user)
        or (runner.scope.kind = organization and job.run.repository.owner_org = runner.scope.owner_org)
    requires: actions_unit_enabled(job.run.repository)
    requires: runner.labels.count > 0 and job.runs_on.count > 0
    requires: (job.runs_on - runner.labels).count = 0
    requires: not (runner.is_ephemeral and runner.has_taken_task)
    requires: config.concurrency_group_queue_enabled implies not blocked_by_concurrency_group(job.run)
    ensures: Task.created(
        job: job,
        runner: runner,
        attempt: job.attempt,
        status: running,
        started_at: now,
        stopped_at: null,
        last_activity_at: now,
        token: new_secret_token(),
        request_key: request_key,
        is_fork_pull_request: job.run.is_fork_pull_request,
        oidc_enabled: job.oidc_requested and not job.run.secrets_withheld,
        log_length: 0,
        log_size: 0,
        log_archived: false,
        log_expired: false
    )
    ensures:
        job.status = running
        job.is_assigned = true
        job.started_at = now
        job.status_changed_at = now
        runner.has_taken_task = true
        runner.is_busy = true
        runner.last_online_at = now
        if job.run.started_at = null:
            job.run.started_at = now
        WorkflowJobStatusChanged(job, prior_status: waiting)
    @guidance
        -- Order: run priority (highest first), then the job's last update,
        -- then creation order — i.e. FIFO unless a run was prioritised.
        -- A run is blocked by its concurrency group when another run of the
        -- same group is running, or is pending with a lower index.
        -- A runner may ask for a specific job attempt by its handle, and may
        -- ask for several tasks at once up to its declared capacity.
        -- The task payload carries the job's workflow, the git context, the
        -- variables, the secrets (none for fork pull requests other than
        -- pull_request_target; FORGEJO_TOKEN always), the needed jobs'
        -- outputs and results, and a runtime token (24h) for artifacts and
        -- ID tokens. Steps are created from the job definition as waiting.
}

-- A retried fetch with the same request key gets the same tasks back,
-- each with a newly minted token.
-- from: routers/api/actions/runner/runner.go:385
rule RunnerRecoversTasks {
    when: RunnerRetriesFetch(runner, request_key)
    ensures:
        for task in runner.tasks where request_key = request_key:
            task.token = new_secret_token()
        runner.last_online_at = now
}

-- Progress report without a result: refreshes liveness and step states.
-- from: services/actions/task.go:323
rule RunnerReportsProgress {
    when: RunnerReportsTaskProgress(runner, task)
    requires: task.runner = runner
    requires: task.status = running
    ensures:
        task.last_activity_at = now
        runner.last_online_at = now
        runner.last_active_at = now
}

-- Final report: task, job and (eventually) run take the result. An
-- ephemeral runner is deleted as soon as it has reported its result.
-- from: services/actions/task.go:323
rule RunnerReportsResult {
    when: RunnerReportsTaskResult(runner, task, result)
    requires: task.runner = runner
    requires: task.status = running
    requires: result in {success, failure, cancelled, skipped}
    ensures:
        task.status = result
        task.stopped_at = now
        task.last_activity_at = now
        task.job.status = result
        task.job.stopped_at = now
        task.job.status_changed_at = now
        WorkflowJobCompleted(job: task.job, prior_status: running)
        runner.is_busy = false
        runner.last_online_at = now
        runner.last_active_at = now
        if runner.is_ephemeral:
            not exists runner
    @guidance
        -- Reports for a task that is already finished are acknowledged and
        -- change nothing (the task may have been cancelled meanwhile).
        -- A finished task makes the job emitter re-check blocked jobs.
}

-- from: routers/api/actions/runner/runner.go:258
rule RunnerReportsOutput {
    when: RunnerReportsTaskOutput(runner, task, key, value)
    requires: task.runner = runner
    requires: output_within_limits(key, value)
    requires: existing_output(task, key) = null
    ensures: TaskOutput.created(task: task, key: key, value: value)
    @guidance
        -- output_within_limits: key at most 255 characters, value at most 1 MiB;
        -- oversize outputs are silently dropped.
}

-- from: routers/api/actions/runner/runner.go:300
rule RunnerAppendsLog {
    when: RunnerAppendsTaskLog(runner, task, from_index, row_count, byte_count, no_more)
    requires: task.runner = runner
    requires: not task.log_archived
    requires: from_index <= task.log_length
    let new_rows = from_index + row_count - task.log_length
    ensures:
        if new_rows > 0:
            task.log_length = task.log_length + new_rows
            task.log_size = task.log_size + byte_count
        if no_more:
            task.log_archived = true
        runner.last_online_at = now
        runner.last_active_at = now
    @guidance
        -- Each line is stored with its timestamp and truncated to 64 KiB.
        -- Archived logs are compressed with zstd unless LOG_COMPRESSION=none.
}

-- from: routers/api/actions/runner/runner.go:345
rule RunnerSubmitsStepSummary {
    when: RunnerSubmitsStepSummary(runner, step, content)
    requires: step.task.runner = runner
    ensures: step.summary = truncate_to_bytes(content, config.max_step_summary_bytes)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: users acting on runs and workflows
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: routers/web/repo/actions/view.go:633
rule UserCancelsRun {
    when: UserCancelsWorkflowRun(user, run)
    requires: can_write_actions(user, run.repository)
    requires: run.status in {waiting, blocked, running}
    ensures: RunKillRequested(run, as_failure: false)
}

-- Re-run all jobs of a finished, valid run whose workflow is not disabled.
-- Artifacts of the previous attempt are discarded.
-- from: services/actions/rerun.go:50
rule UserRerunsRun {
    when: UserRerunsWorkflowRun(user, run)
    requires: can_write_actions(user, run.repository)
    requires: run.pre_execution_error = null
    requires: run.status in {success, failure, cancelled, skipped}
    requires: not workflow_disabled(run.repository, run.workflow_file)
    ensures:
        run.previous_attempts_duration = run.previous_attempts_duration + run_duration(run)
        run.status = waiting
        run.started_at = null
        run.stopped_at = null
        run.attempt = run.attempt + 1
        run.priority = 0
        run.prioritized = false
        for artifact in run.artifacts where status in {upload_pending, upload_confirmed, expired}:
            artifact.status = pending_deletion
        for job in run.jobs:
            job.attempt = job.attempt + 1
            job.handle = new_handle()
            job.is_assigned = false
            job.started_at = null
            job.stopped_at = null
            job.status_changed_at = now
            if job.needs.count > 0:
                job.status = blocked
            else:
                job.status = waiting
            WorkflowJobAttemptStarted(job)
        WorkflowRunAttemptStarted(run)
}

-- Re-run one finished job plus every job that (transitively) needs it;
-- unfinished dependants are cancelled first. The chosen job starts waiting
-- even if it has needs. The whole run's artifacts are discarded.
-- from: services/actions/rerun.go:118
rule UserRerunsJob {
    when: UserRerunsWorkflowJob(user, job)
    requires: can_write_actions(user, job.run.repository)
    requires: job.run.pre_execution_error = null
    requires: job.status in {success, failure, cancelled, skipped}
    requires: not workflow_disabled(job.run.repository, job.run.workflow_file)
    ensures:
        for artifact in job.run.artifacts where status in {upload_pending, upload_confirmed, expired}:
            artifact.status = pending_deletion
        for dependant in dependants_of(job):
            JobRerunRequested(job: dependant, keep_blocked: true)
        JobRerunRequested(job, keep_blocked: false)
        if job.run.status in {success, failure, cancelled, skipped}:
            job.run.attempt = job.run.attempt + 1
            WorkflowRunAttemptStarted(run: job.run)
}

-- from: services/actions/job.go:20
rule RerunSingleJob {
    when: JobRerunRequested(job, keep_blocked)
    ensures:
        for task in job.tasks where status = running:
            TaskStopRequested(task, as_failure: false)
        job.attempt = job.attempt + 1
        job.handle = new_handle()
        job.is_assigned = false
        job.started_at = null
        job.stopped_at = null
        job.status_changed_at = now
        if keep_blocked and job.needs.count > 0:
            job.status = blocked
        else:
            job.status = waiting
        WorkflowJobAttemptStarted(job)
}

-- Only finished runs can be deleted; logs, tasks and artifacts go with it.
-- from: services/actions/run.go:310
rule UserDeletesRun {
    when: UserDeletesWorkflowRun(user, run)
    requires: is_repo_admin(user, run.repository)
    requires: run.status in {success, failure, cancelled, skipped}
    ensures:
        for artifact in run.artifacts where status in {upload_pending, upload_confirmed, expired}:
            artifact.status = pending_deletion
        for job in run.jobs:
            for task in job.tasks:
                not exists task
            not exists job
        not exists run
}

-- from: services/actions/run.go:345
rule UserPrioritizesRun {
    when: UserPrioritizesWorkflowRun(user, run)
    requires: can_write_actions(user, run.repository)
    requires: run.status in {waiting, blocked}
    requires: not run.prioritized
    ensures:
        run.prioritized = true
        run.priority = 127
}

-- from: services/actions/run.go:370
rule UserDeprioritizesRun {
    when: UserDeprioritizesWorkflowRun(user, run)
    requires: can_write_actions(user, run.repository)
    requires: run.prioritized
    ensures:
        run.prioritized = false
        run.priority = 0
}

-- A disabled workflow starts no event-driven or scheduled runs and cannot
-- be re-run.
-- from: routers/web/repo/actions/view.go:880
rule UserDisablesWorkflow {
    when: UserDisablesWorkflowFile(user, workflow)
    requires: is_repo_admin(user, workflow.repository)
    ensures: workflow.is_disabled = true
}

-- from: routers/web/repo/actions/view.go:880
rule UserEnablesWorkflow {
    when: UserEnablesWorkflowFile(user, workflow)
    requires: is_repo_admin(user, workflow.repository)
    ensures: workflow.is_disabled = false
}

-- Manual dispatch of a workflow that declares `workflow_dispatch`, at any
-- branch or tag. Missing inputs take their defaults; a required input
-- with neither value nor default refuses the dispatch.
-- from: services/actions/workflows.go:79
rule UserDispatchesWorkflow {
    when: UserDispatchesWorkflowRun(user, workflow, ref, inputs)
    requires: can_write_actions(user, workflow.repository)
    requires: not workflow.repository.is_archived
    requires: not workflow.repository.is_empty
    requires: ref_exists(workflow.repository, ref)
    requires: workflow.has_dispatch_trigger
    requires: required_inputs_present(workflow, inputs)
    requires: inputs.count <= config.limit_dispatch_inputs
    ensures: WorkflowRun.created(
        repository: workflow.repository,
        index: next_run_index(workflow.repository),
        title: dispatch_title(workflow),
        workflow_file: workflow.file_name,
        workflow_directory: workflow.directory,
        trigger_user: user,
        event: workflow_dispatch,
        trigger_event: workflow_dispatch,
        activity: null,
        ref: ref,
        commit_sha: ref_commit(workflow.repository, ref),
        workflow_source_sha: null,
        schedule: null,
        inputs: inputs,
        status: waiting,
        created_at: now,
        started_at: null,
        stopped_at: null,
        previous_attempts_duration: 0.seconds,
        attempt: 1,
        notify_email: workflow_notifies_by_email(workflow),
        pull_request: null,
        pull_request_poster: null,
        is_fork_pull_request: false,
        needs_approval: false,
        approved_by: null,
        concurrency_group: concurrency_group_for_dispatch(workflow, ref, inputs),
        concurrency_mode: concurrency_mode_for_dispatch(workflow, inputs),
        pre_execution_error: null,
        pre_execution_error_details: null,
        has_permissions_warning: declares_permissions(workflow),
        priority: 0,
        prioritized: false,
        jobs_expanded: false
    )
    @guidance
        -- required_inputs_present: every input marked required has a value
        -- or a default. Web: form fields inputs[<key>]; API: JSON inputs map,
        -- optional return_run_info. Boolean inputs are passed as
        -- "true"/"false". The title is the workflow `name:` (else its path),
        -- replaced by `run-name:` when that evaluates non-empty.
        -- Forgejo does not refuse dispatching a disabled workflow (see open
        -- questions).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: artifacts
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A running job creates (or re-opens) an artifact of its run with the
-- instance's default retention.
-- from: models/actions/artifact.go:58
rule TaskCreatesArtifact {
    when: TaskCreatesArtifact(task, name)
    requires: task.status = running
    requires: quota_allows_artifacts(task.job.run.repository)
    ensures: Artifact.created(
        run: task.job.run,
        name: name,
        uploaded_by: task,
        size: 0,
        compressed_size: 0,
        status: upload_pending,
        created_at: now,
        expires_at: now + config.artifact_retention
    )
}

-- The job may ask for its own retention (in days, or an expiry time).
-- from: routers/api/actions/artifactsv4.go:284
rule TaskCreatesArtifactWithRetention {
    when: TaskCreatesArtifactWithRetention(task, name, retention)
    requires: task.status = running
    requires: quota_allows_artifacts(task.job.run.repository)
    ensures: Artifact.created(
        run: task.job.run,
        name: name,
        uploaded_by: task,
        size: 0,
        compressed_size: 0,
        status: upload_pending,
        created_at: now,
        expires_at: now + retention
    )
}

-- from: routers/api/actions/artifacts_chunks.go:295
rule TaskFinalizesArtifact {
    when: TaskFinalizesArtifact(task, artifact, size)
    requires: task.status = running
    requires: artifact.run = task.job.run
    requires: artifact.status = upload_pending
    ensures:
        artifact.status = upload_confirmed
        artifact.size = size
        artifact.compressed_size = stored_size(artifact)
}

-- from: routers/web/repo/actions/view.go:761
rule UserDeletesArtifact {
    when: UserDeletesRunArtifact(user, artifact)
    requires: can_write_actions(user, artifact.run.repository)
    requires: artifact.status = upload_confirmed
    ensures: artifact.status = pending_deletion
}

-- from: services/actions/cleanup.go:48
rule ArtifactExpires {
    when: artifact: Artifact.expires_at <= now
    requires: artifact.status = upload_confirmed
    ensures: ArtifactExpiryDue(artifact)
}

-- from: services/actions/cleanup.go:48
rule ExpireArtifact {
    when: ArtifactExpiryDue(artifact)
    requires: artifact.status = upload_confirmed
    ensures: artifact.status = expired
    @guidance
        -- Content is removed from storage; the record stays listed as expired.
        -- Swept by the daily cleanup_actions cron.
}

-- from: services/actions/cleanup.go:70
rule ArtifactPurged {
    when: artifact: Artifact.status becomes pending_deletion
    ensures: ArtifactPurgeDue(artifact)
}

-- from: services/actions/cleanup.go:70
rule PurgeArtifact {
    when: ArtifactPurgeDue(artifact)
    requires: artifact.status = pending_deletion
    ensures: artifact.status = deleted
    @guidance
        -- Performed by the daily cleanup_actions cron, in batches of 100.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: logs
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/actions/cleanup.go:96
rule TaskLogsExpire {
    when: task: Task.stopped_at + config.log_retention <= now
    requires: not task.log_expired
    ensures: TaskLogExpiryDue(task)
}

-- from: services/actions/cleanup.go:96
rule ExpireTaskLog {
    when: TaskLogExpiryDue(task)
    requires: not task.log_expired
    ensures: task.log_expired = true
}

-- Finished tasks whose runner never said "no more" get their logs archived.
-- from: services/actions/log.go:25
rule LingeringLogArchived {
    when: task: Task.stopped_at + config.lingering_log_age <= now
    requires: not task.log_archived
    requires: not task.log_expired
    ensures: LingeringLogTransferDue(task)
}

-- from: services/actions/log.go:25
rule ArchiveLingeringLog {
    when: LingeringLogTransferDue(task)
    requires: not task.log_archived
    requires: not task.log_expired
    ensures: task.log_archived = true
    @guidance
        -- Nightly, at most 3000 tasks per pass, paced to spare the storage.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: liveness clean-up
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A running task that has not reported anything for too long fails.
-- from: services/actions/clear_tasks.go:22
rule ZombieTaskFails {
    when: task: Task.last_activity_at + config.zombie_task_timeout <= now
    requires: task.status = running
    ensures: TaskTimedOut(task)
}

-- A running task that has run for too long fails even if it reports.
-- from: services/actions/clear_tasks.go:30
rule EndlessTaskFails {
    when: task: Task.started_at + config.endless_task_timeout <= now
    requires: task.status = running
    ensures: TaskTimedOut(task)
}

-- from: services/actions/task.go:257
rule TimedOutTaskFailsItsJob {
    when: TaskTimedOut(task)
    requires: task.status = running
    ensures:
        task.status = failure
        task.stopped_at = now
        task.runner.is_busy = false
        for step in task.steps where status in {waiting, blocked, running}:
            step.status = failure
            step.stopped_at = now
        task.job.status = failure
        task.job.stopped_at = now
        task.job.status_changed_at = now
        WorkflowJobCompleted(job: task.job, prior_status: running)
}

-- A job nobody picked up (or that stayed blocked) for too long is
-- cancelled, unless its run is still waiting for approval.
-- from: services/actions/clear_tasks.go:85
rule AbandonedJobCancelled {
    when: job: Job.status_changed_at + config.abandoned_job_timeout <= now
    requires: job.status in {waiting, blocked}
    requires: not job.run.needs_approval
    ensures: JobAbandoned(job)
}

-- from: services/actions/clear_tasks.go:85
rule CancelAbandonedJob {
    when: JobAbandoned(job)
    requires: job.status in {waiting, blocked}
    requires: not job.run.needs_approval
    ensures:
        job.status = cancelled
        job.stopped_at = now
        job.status_changed_at = now
        WorkflowJobCompleted(job, prior_status: waiting)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: commit statuses
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Every job of a push, pull_request(_target) or release run reports a
-- commit status "<workflow name> / <job name> (<event>)" on the relevant
-- commit (push head, pull request head, release commit).
-- from: services/actions/commit_status.go:31
rule ReportJobCommitStatusOnChange {
    when: WorkflowJobStatusChanged(job, prior_status)
    requires: job.run.event in {push, pull_request, pull_request_sync, pull_request_label,
        pull_request_assign, pull_request_milestone, release}
    requires: not job.is_incomplete
    ensures: code/CommitStatusReported(repository: job.run.repository, commit_sha: status_commit(job.run),
        context: commit_status_context(job), state: commit_state(job.status), target_url: job_link(job),
        description: commit_status_description(job), creator: actions_bot())
}

-- from: services/actions/commit_status.go:31
rule ReportJobCommitStatusOnCompletion {
    when: WorkflowJobCompleted(job, prior_status)
    requires: job.run.event in {push, pull_request, pull_request_sync, pull_request_label,
        pull_request_assign, pull_request_milestone, release}
    requires: not job.is_incomplete
    ensures: code/CommitStatusReported(repository: job.run.repository, commit_sha: status_commit(job.run),
        context: commit_status_context(job), state: commit_state(job.status), target_url: job_link(job),
        description: commit_status_description(job), creator: actions_bot())
    @guidance
        -- success -> success ("Successful in <duration>"), failure and
        -- cancelled -> failure, skipped -> skipped, waiting/blocked/running ->
        -- pending ("Waiting to run" / "Blocked by required conditions" /
        -- "Has started running"). An identical latest status is not repeated.
}

-- from: services/actions/commit_status.go:31
rule ReportJobCommitStatusOnAttempt {
    when: WorkflowJobAttemptStarted(job)
    requires: job.run.event in {push, pull_request, pull_request_sync, pull_request_label,
        pull_request_assign, pull_request_milestone, release}
    requires: not job.is_incomplete
    ensures: code/CommitStatusReported(repository: job.run.repository, commit_sha: status_commit(job.run),
        context: commit_status_context(job), state: commit_state(job.status), target_url: job_link(job),
        description: commit_status_description(job), creator: actions_bot())
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: OIDC ID tokens
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A job that enabled OpenID Connect may exchange its runtime token for a
-- signed ID token describing the run (repository, ref, sha, actor, event,
-- workflow, run id/number/attempt). The audience defaults to the
-- repository owner's URL.
-- from: routers/api/actions/id_token.go:98
rule TaskRequestsIdToken {
    when: TaskRequestsIdToken(task, audience)
    requires: task.status = running
    requires: task.oidc_enabled
    ensures: IdTokenIssued(task, audience, expires_at: now + config.id_token_lifetime)
    @guidance
        -- An empty audience means the repository owner's URL.
        -- `sub` is "repo:<owner>-<owner_id>/<repo>-<repo_id>:pull_request"
        -- for pull_request events, else "...:ref:<ref>"; a per-repository
        -- legacy format omits the ids. Public keys are published at a JWKS
        -- endpoint with an OpenID discovery document.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: secrets and variables
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Create a secret, or overwrite the value of the one with that name
-- (names are case-insensitive).
-- from: services/secrets/secrets.go:13
rule UserSetsSecret {
    when: UserSetsActionsSecret(user, scope, name, value)
    requires: may_manage_actions_scope(user, scope)
    requires: scope.kind != instance
    requires: valid_secret_name(name)
    let existing = existing_secret(scope, name)
    ensures:
        if existing != null:
            existing.value = value
        else:
            Secret.created(scope: scope, name: upper(name), value: value, created_at: now)
    @guidance
        -- valid_secret_name: [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*, not starting with
        -- FORGEJO_, GITEA_ or GITHUB_ (case-insensitive). Line breaks are
        -- normalised to \n. The value is encrypted at rest and never
        -- returned by any interface.
}

-- from: services/secrets/secrets.go:47
rule UserDeletesSecret {
    when: UserDeletesActionsSecret(user, secret)
    requires: may_manage_actions_scope(user, secret.scope)
    ensures: not exists secret
}

-- from: services/actions/variables.go:17
rule UserCreatesVariable {
    when: UserCreatesActionsVariable(user, scope, name, value)
    requires: may_manage_actions_scope(user, scope)
    requires: valid_variable_name(name)
    requires: existing_variable(scope, name) = null
    ensures: Variable.created(scope: scope, name: upper(name), value: value,
        created_at: now, updated_at: null)
    @guidance
        -- valid_variable_name: the secret-name rules, and not "CI".
        -- Line breaks are normalised to \n.
}

-- from: services/actions/variables.go:30
rule UserUpdatesVariable {
    when: UserUpdatesActionsVariable(user, variable, name, value)
    requires: may_manage_actions_scope(user, variable.scope)
    requires: valid_variable_name(name)
    ensures:
        variable.name = upper(name)
        variable.value = value
        variable.updated_at = now
}

-- from: services/actions/variables.go:47
rule UserDeletesVariable {
    when: UserDeletesActionsVariable(user, variable)
    requires: may_manage_actions_scope(user, variable.scope)
    ensures: not exists variable
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: scheduled workflows
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Re-register a repository's schedules from its default branch head:
-- all existing schedules are replaced.
-- from: services/actions/notifier_helper.go:576
rule RefreshSchedules {
    when: SchedulesNeedRefresh(repository)
    requires: config.actions_enabled
    requires: actions_unit_enabled(repository)
    requires: not repository.is_empty
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    ensures:
        for old in Schedules where repository = repository:
            for spec in old.specs:
                not exists spec
            not exists old
        for workflow in scheduled_workflows(repository):
            ScheduleRegistrationRequested(workflow)
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier_helper.go:600
rule RegisterSchedule {
    when: ScheduleRegistrationRequested(workflow)
    ensures: Schedule.created(
        repository: workflow.repository,
        workflow_file: workflow.file_name,
        workflow_directory: workflow.directory,
        title: dispatch_title(workflow),
        ref: "refs/heads/" + workflow.repository.default_branch,
        commit_sha: default_branch_head(workflow.repository),
        created_at: now
    )
    @guidance
        -- One ScheduleSpec per `cron:` entry, next_run_at = next match after
        -- now, in the workflow's `timezone:` (else a TZ=/CRON_TZ= prefix,
        -- else UTC). Triggered by the Actions bot, never by a person.
}

-- from: services/actions/notifier.go:600
rule DefaultBranchChangeRefreshesSchedules {
    when: code/DefaultBranchChanged(repository, old_name, new_name, by)
    ensures: SchedulesNeedRefresh(repository)
}

-- Renaming the default branch re-registers schedules against the new name.
-- from: services/repository/branch.go:430
rule DefaultBranchRenameRefreshesSchedules {
    when: code/BranchRenamed(repository, from_name, to_name, by)
    requires: to_name = repository.default_branch
    ensures: SchedulesNeedRefresh(repository)
}

-- from: routers/web/repo/setting/setting.go:1088
rule UnarchiveRefreshesSchedules {
    when: repositories/RepositoryUnarchived(repository, doer)
    ensures: SchedulesNeedRefresh(repository)
}

-- from: services/repository/setting.go:38
rule ActionsUnitEnabledRefreshesSchedules {
    when: repositories/RepoUnitEnabled(repository, kind)
    requires: kind = actions
    ensures: SchedulesNeedRefresh(repository)
}

-- from: routers/web/repo/setting/setting.go:1065
rule ArchiveDropsSchedules {
    when: repositories/RepositoryArchived(repository, doer)
    ensures: SchedulesDropped(repository)
}

-- from: services/repository/setting.go:31
rule ActionsUnitDisabledDropsSchedules {
    when: repositories/RepoUnitDisabled(repository, kind)
    requires: kind = actions
    ensures: SchedulesDropped(repository)
}

-- Schedules go away and unfinished scheduled runs are cancelled.
-- from: services/actions/schedule_tasks.go:283
rule DropSchedules {
    when: SchedulesDropped(repository)
    ensures:
        for old in Schedules where repository = repository:
            for spec in old.specs:
                not exists spec
            not exists old
        for run in WorkflowRuns where repository = repository and trigger_event = schedule
                and status in {waiting, blocked, running}:
            RunKillRequested(run, as_failure: false)
}

-- A due cron entry starts a run of its schedule's workflow, then moves to
-- its next occurrence at least one minute later.
-- from: services/actions/schedule_tasks.go:30
rule ScheduleFires {
    when: spec: ScheduleSpec.next_run_at <= now
    ensures: ScheduleSpecDue(spec)
}

-- A due cron entry of a usable schedule starts its run.
-- from: services/actions/schedule_tasks.go:30
rule StartScheduledRun {
    when: ScheduleSpecDue(spec)
    requires: not spec.schedule.repository.is_archived
    requires: actions_unit_enabled(spec.schedule.repository)
    requires: not workflow_disabled(spec.schedule.repository, spec.schedule.workflow_file)
    requires: not schedule_is_broken(spec)
    ensures: WorkflowRun.created(
        repository: spec.schedule.repository,
        index: next_run_index(spec.schedule.repository),
        title: spec.schedule.title,
        workflow_file: spec.schedule.workflow_file,
        workflow_directory: spec.schedule.workflow_directory,
        trigger_user: actions_bot(),
        event: schedule,
        trigger_event: schedule,
        activity: null,
        ref: spec.schedule.ref,
        commit_sha: spec.schedule.commit_sha,
        workflow_source_sha: null,
        schedule: spec.schedule,
        inputs: {},
        status: waiting,
        created_at: now,
        started_at: null,
        stopped_at: null,
        previous_attempts_duration: 0.seconds,
        attempt: 1,
        notify_email: schedule_notifies_by_email(spec.schedule),
        pull_request: null,
        pull_request_poster: null,
        is_fork_pull_request: false,
        needs_approval: false,
        approved_by: null,
        concurrency_group: concurrency_group_for_schedule(spec.schedule),
        concurrency_mode: concurrency_mode_for_schedule(spec.schedule),
        pre_execution_error: null,
        pre_execution_error_details: null,
        has_permissions_warning: false,
        priority: 0,
        prioritized: false,
        jobs_expanded: false
    )
    ensures:
        spec.previous_run_at = spec.next_run_at
        spec.next_run_at = next_cron_occurrence(spec, now + 1.minute)
    @guidance
        -- Checked every minute (start_schedule_tasks cron). Scheduled runs
        -- report no commit statuses. There is no inactivity-based disabling.
}

-- A cron entry that can never produce a run (unparseable cron, unknown
-- time zone, workflow that no longer parses) disables its workflow.
-- from: services/actions/schedule_tasks.go:94
rule BrokenScheduleDisablesWorkflow {
    when: ScheduleSpecDue(spec)
    requires: schedule_is_broken(spec)
    ensures:
        for workflow in Workflows where repository = spec.schedule.repository
                and file_name = spec.schedule.workflow_file:
            workflow.is_disabled = true
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: deletion cascades
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/repository/delete.go:172
rule RepositoryDeletionRemovesActionsData {
    when: repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)
    ensures:
        for run in WorkflowRuns where repository = repository:
            for artifact in run.artifacts:
                not exists artifact
            for job in run.jobs:
                for task in job.tasks:
                    if task.runner.is_ephemeral:
                        not exists task.runner
                    not exists task
                not exists job
            not exists run
        for schedule in Schedules where repository = repository:
            not exists schedule
        for scope in ActionsScopes where repository = repository:
            for runner in scope.runners:
                not exists runner
            for secret in scope.secrets:
                not exists secret
            for variable in scope.variables:
                not exists variable
            for token in scope.registration_tokens:
                not exists token
        for tc in TrustedContributors where repository = repository:
            not exists tc
        for workflow in Workflows where repository = repository:
            not exists workflow
}

-- from: models/actions/runner.go:357
rule UserDeletionRemovesActionsScope {
    when: accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, purge, delete_contributions)
    ensures:
        for scope in ActionsScopes where owner_user = user:
            for runner in scope.runners:
                not exists runner
            for secret in scope.secrets:
                not exists secret
            for variable in scope.variables:
                not exists variable
            for token in scope.registration_tokens:
                not exists token
        for tc in TrustedContributors where user = user:
            not exists tc
}

-- from: models/actions/runner.go:357
rule OrganizationDeletionRemovesActionsScope {
    when: organizations/OrganizationDeleted(organization)
    ensures:
        for scope in ActionsScopes where owner_org = organization:
            for runner in scope.runners:
                not exists runner
            for secret in scope.secrets:
                not exists secret
            for variable in scope.variables:
                not exists variable
            for token in scope.registration_tokens:
                not exists token
}

-- Blocking a user revokes the trust they had on the blocker's repositories
-- and cancels their unfinished pull-request runs there.
-- from: services/user/block.go:95
rule BlockingRevokesActionsTrust {
    when: accounts/UserBlocked(blocker, blocked)
    ensures:
        for tc in TrustedContributors where user = blocked and repository.owner_user = blocker:
            not exists tc
        for run in WorkflowRuns where pull_request_poster = blocked and repository.owner_user = blocker
                and status in {waiting, blocked, running}:
            RunKillRequested(run, as_failure: false)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: scheduled tasks dispatched by administration
------------------------------------------------------------
-- Administration's cron (and its "run now" button) emits one trigger per
-- task. Each sweep below emits, for every item that is due, the same
-- internal trigger the matching temporal rule emits, so the work itself is
-- described once (TimedOutTaskFailsItsJob, CancelAbandonedJob,
-- ArchiveLingeringLog, StartScheduledRun / BrokenScheduleDisablesWorkflow,
-- ExpireArtifact, PurgeArtifact, ExpireTaskLog, RemoveSweptRunner,
-- RevokeLapsedTrust).

-- from: services/cron/tasks_actions.go:30
rule ZombieTaskSweep {
    when: administration/ZombieActionsTaskStopDue()
    ensures:
        for task in Tasks where status = running and last_activity_at + config.zombie_task_timeout <= now:
            TaskTimedOut(task)
}

-- from: services/cron/tasks_actions.go:40
rule EndlessTaskSweep {
    when: administration/EndlessActionsTaskStopDue()
    ensures:
        for task in Tasks where status = running and started_at + config.endless_task_timeout <= now:
            TaskTimedOut(task)
}

-- from: services/cron/tasks_actions.go:50
rule AbandonedJobSweep {
    when: administration/AbandonedActionsJobCancellationDue()
    ensures:
        for job in Jobs where status in {waiting, blocked} and not run.needs_approval
                and status_changed_at + config.abandoned_job_timeout <= now:
            JobAbandoned(job)
}

-- from: services/cron/tasks_actions.go:60
rule LingeringLogSweep {
    when: administration/LingeringActionsLogTransferDue()
    ensures:
        for task in Tasks where stopped_at != null and not log_archived and not log_expired
                and stopped_at + config.lingering_log_age <= now:
            LingeringLogTransferDue(task)
}

-- from: services/cron/tasks_actions.go:72
rule ScheduleSweep {
    when: administration/ActionsScheduleStartDue()
    ensures:
        for spec in ScheduleSpecs where next_run_at <= now:
            ScheduleSpecDue(spec)
}

-- Expired and deleted artifacts, expired logs and used ephemeral runners.
-- from: services/actions/cleanup.go:25
rule ActionsCleanupSweep {
    when: administration/ActionsCleanupDue()
    ensures:
        for artifact in Artifacts where status = upload_confirmed and expires_at <= now:
            ArtifactExpiryDue(artifact)
        for artifact in Artifacts where status = pending_deletion:
            ArtifactPurgeDue(artifact)
        for task in Tasks where stopped_at != null and not log_expired
                and stopped_at + config.log_retention <= now:
            TaskLogExpiryDue(task)
        for runner in Runners where has_used_its_single_task and not is_busy:
            RunnerRemovalDue(runner)
}

-- Trust that has not been relied upon within the expiry lapses.
-- from: services/actions/trust.go:31
rule TrustedContributorSweep {
    when: administration/ActionsUserCleanupDue()
    ensures:
        for tc in TrustedContributors where last_access_at + config.trusted_contributor_expiry <= now:
            TrustedContributorLapsed(trusted_contributor: tc)
}

-- The task's own arguments decide the age and whether only instance-wide
-- runners are swept.
-- from: services/actions/cleanup.go:166
rule OfflineRunnerSweep {
    when: administration/OfflineRunnerCleanupDue(older_than, global_scope_only)
    ensures:
        for runner in Runners where created_at + older_than <= now
                and (last_online_at = null or last_online_at + older_than <= now)
                and (global_scope_only implies scope.kind = instance):
            RunnerRemovalDue(runner)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant UniqueRunIndexPerRepository {
    for a in WorkflowRuns:
        for b in WorkflowRuns:
            a != b and a.repository = b.repository implies a.index != b.index
}

invariant UniqueSecretNamePerScope {
    for a in Secrets:
        for b in Secrets:
            a != b and a.scope = b.scope implies a.name != b.name
}

invariant UniqueVariableNamePerScope {
    for a in Variables:
        for b in Variables:
            a != b and a.scope = b.scope implies a.name != b.name
}

invariant AtMostOneActiveRegistrationTokenPerScope {
    for s in ActionsScopes:
        s.active_registration_tokens.count <= 1
}

invariant UniqueArtifactNamePerRun {
    for a in Artifacts:
        for b in Artifacts:
            a != b and a.run = b.run and a.status != deleted and b.status != deleted implies a.name != b.name
}

invariant OneTaskPerJobAttempt {
    for a in Tasks:
        for b in Tasks:
            a != b and a.job = b.job implies a.attempt != b.attempt
}

invariant EphemeralRunnerRunsAtMostOneTask {
    for r in Runners:
        r.is_ephemeral implies r.tasks.count <= 1
}

invariant RunningJobHasRunningTask {
    for j in Jobs:
        j.status = running implies j.tasks.any(t => t.attempt = j.attempt)
}

invariant ApprovalOnlyForPullRequests {
    for r in WorkflowRuns:
        r.needs_approval implies r.pull_request != null
}

invariant OutputKeyUniquePerTask {
    for a in TaskOutputs:
        for b in TaskOutputs:
            a != b and a.task = b.task implies a.key != b.key
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Someone with read access to the Actions unit of the run's repository.
-- (= access/can_read(user, repository, actions); Actions enabled on the
-- instance and not globally disabled as a unit.)
actor RunViewer {
    within: WorkflowRun
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_read_actions(this, within.repository)
}

-- Someone with read access to the Actions unit of the task's repository.
actor TaskViewer {
    within: Task
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_read_actions(this, within.job.run.repository)
}

-- Someone with read access to the Actions unit of the workflow's repository.
actor WorkflowViewer {
    within: Workflow
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_read_actions(this, within.repository)
}

-- Whoever may manage a scope's runners, secrets and variables.
actor ScopeManager {
    within: ActionsScope
    identified_by: accounts/User where may_manage_actions_scope(this, within)
}

-- Whoever may approve or deny a pull request's runs: repository admin, site
-- admin, or write access to the Actions unit.
actor TrustDelegate {
    within: pulls/PullRequest
    identified_by: accounts/User where may_delegate_actions_trust(this, within.base_repository)
}

-- A runner that has registered and authenticates with its runner token.
actor RegisteredRunner {
    identified_by: Runner where token != ""
}

-- The holder of a running task's automatic or runtime token (the job itself).
actor RunningJob {
    identified_by: Task where status = running
}

-- A runner agent that is not registered yet; it only holds a registration token.
actor UnregisteredRunnerAgent {
    identified_by: RunnerRegistrationToken where is_active = true
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The Actions tab of a repository: workflows and their runs.
-- Web: GET /{owner}/{repo}/actions?workflow=&actor=&status=,
--      POST /actions/disable|enable?workflow=, POST /actions/manual,
--      GET /actions/workflows/{file}/badge.svg, /actions/workflows/{file}/runs/latest
-- API: GET /repos/{o}/{r}/actions/runs (filters event, status, run_number,
--      head_sha, ref, workflow_id), GET /actions/tasks,
--      POST /actions/workflows/{file}/dispatches
-- from: routers/web/web.go:1654
surface RepositoryWorkflows {
    facing viewer: WorkflowViewer
    context workflow: Workflow

    exposes:
        workflow.file_name
        workflow.path
        workflow.name
        workflow.is_disabled
        workflow.has_dispatch_trigger
        workflow.has_schedule_trigger
        workflow.dispatch_inputs when workflow.has_dispatch_trigger
        workflow_badge_status(workflow)

    provides:
        UserDispatchesWorkflowRun(viewer, workflow, ref, inputs)
            when can_write_actions(viewer, workflow.repository) and workflow.has_dispatch_trigger
        UserDisablesWorkflowFile(viewer, workflow)
            when is_repo_admin(viewer, workflow.repository) and not workflow.is_disabled
        UserEnablesWorkflowFile(viewer, workflow)
            when is_repo_admin(viewer, workflow.repository) and workflow.is_disabled

    related:
        WorkflowRunPage(latest_run(workflow)) when latest_run(workflow) != null

    contracts:
        demands WorkflowParser

    @guidance
        -- The run list shows, per run: title, workflow, index, event, ref
        -- (a deleted ref is marked), commit, trigger user, status, duration.
        -- The badge shows the latest run's status for a workflow (optionally
        -- per branch / event).
}

-- One run with its jobs, attempts, logs, summaries and artifacts.
-- Web: /actions/runs/{index}[/jobs/{j}[/attempt/{n}[/logs]]], POST cancel,
--      rerun, jobs/{j}/rerun, delete, prioritize, deprioritize,
--      GET/DELETE artifacts/{name}
-- API: GET/DELETE /actions/runs/{id}, POST /runs/{id}/cancel|rerun,
--      GET /runs/{id}/jobs|logs|artifacts, GET /actions/jobs/{id}[/logs],
--      POST /actions/jobs/{id}/rerun, GET/DELETE /actions/artifacts/{id}[/zip]
-- from: routers/web/repo/actions/view.go:272
surface WorkflowRunPage {
    facing viewer: RunViewer
    context run: WorkflowRun

    exposes:
        run.title
        run.index
        run.status
        run.event
        run.trigger_event
        run.ref
        run.commit_sha
        run.trigger_user
        run.attempt
        run.created_at
        run.started_at
        run.stopped_at
        run.is_scheduled
        run.is_dispatched
        run.needs_approval
        run.pre_execution_error when run.pre_execution_error != null
        run.has_permissions_warning
        run.prioritized
        run.secrets_withheld
        for job in run.jobs:
            job.name
            job.status
            job.attempt
            job.needs
            job.runs_on
            job.started_at
            job.stopped_at
        for artifact in run.artifacts:
            artifact.name when artifact.status in {upload_confirmed, expired}
            artifact.status when artifact.status in {upload_confirmed, expired}
            artifact.size when artifact.status = upload_confirmed
            artifact.expires_at when artifact.status = upload_confirmed

    provides:
        UserCancelsWorkflowRun(viewer, run)
            when can_write_actions(viewer, run.repository) and run.status in {waiting, blocked, running}
        UserRerunsWorkflowRun(viewer, run)
            when can_write_actions(viewer, run.repository) and run.can_be_rerun
        UserRerunsWorkflowJob(viewer, job)
            when can_write_actions(viewer, run.repository)
        UserDeletesWorkflowRun(viewer, run)
            when is_repo_admin(viewer, run.repository) and run.is_done
        UserPrioritizesWorkflowRun(viewer, run)
            when can_write_actions(viewer, run.repository) and not run.prioritized
        UserDeprioritizesWorkflowRun(viewer, run)
            when can_write_actions(viewer, run.repository) and run.prioritized
        UserDeletesRunArtifact(viewer, artifact)
            when can_write_actions(viewer, run.repository)

    related:
        PullRequestActionsTrust(run.pull_request) when run.pull_request != null
        JobAttemptView(job_latest_task(run)) when job_latest_task(run) != null

    @guidance
        -- Artifact download (zip) needs only read access and only works for
        -- upload_confirmed artifacts. Log download serves one attempt's log
        -- as a text file; a run's logs can be fetched as one zip; expired
        -- logs are reported as cleaned up. Secrets never appear: the runner
        -- masks secret values in logs.
}

-- One attempt of one job: its steps, log and step summaries.
-- Web: /actions/runs/{index}/jobs/{j}/attempt/{n} (POST returns steps and
--      log lines from a cursor for live streaming), .../logs (download)
-- API: GET /actions/jobs/{id}, GET /actions/jobs/{id}/logs
-- from: routers/web/repo/actions/view.go:272
surface JobAttemptView {
    facing viewer: TaskViewer
    context task: Task

    exposes:
        task.job.name
        task.attempt
        task.status
        task.started_at
        task.stopped_at
        task.runner.name
        task.log_length when not task.log_expired
        task.log_size when not task.log_expired
        for step in task.steps:
            step.name
            step.status
            step.started_at
            step.stopped_at
            step.log_length when not task.log_expired
            step.summary

    @guidance
        -- Live view: the page polls with a per-step cursor and receives new
        -- log lines while the task runs; finished logs are read from the
        -- archive. Expired logs are reported as cleaned up.
}

-- The trust panel on a pull request whose runs need approval.
-- Web: POST /{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{index}/action-user-trust (trust=once|always|deny|revoke)
-- from: routers/web/repo/pull.go:2052
surface PullRequestActionsTrust {
    facing maintainer: TrustDelegate
    context pull_request: pulls/PullRequest

    exposes:
        pull_request.issue.poster
        poster_is_trusted(pull_request)
        runs_awaiting_approval(pull_request)

    provides:
        UserApprovesPullRequestRunsOnce(maintainer, pull_request)
        UserAlwaysTrustsPullRequestPoster(maintainer, pull_request)
        UserDeniesPullRequestRuns(maintainer, pull_request)
        UserRevokesPullRequestPosterTrust(maintainer, pull_request)
}

-- Runners, secrets and variables of a scope.
-- Web: /{owner}/{repo}/settings/actions/{runners,secrets,variables},
--      /org/{org}/settings/actions/..., /user/settings/actions/...,
--      /-/admin/actions/{runners,variables} (no instance secrets)
-- API: /repos/{o}/{r}/actions/{secrets,variables,runners}, /orgs/{org}/actions/...,
--      /user/actions/..., /admin/actions/runners, .../runners/registration-token,
--      .../runners/jobs (waiting jobs a runner of this scope could pick)
-- from: routers/web/web.go:617
surface ActionsSettings {
    facing manager: ScopeManager
    context scope: ActionsScope

    exposes:
        scope.kind
        for secret in scope.secrets:
            secret.name
            secret.created_at
        for variable in scope.variables:
            variable.name
            variable.value
            variable.updated_at
        for runner in scope.runners:
            runner.name
            runner.description
            runner.labels
            runner.version
            runner.health
            runner.is_ephemeral
            runner.last_online_at
        inherited_runners(scope)
        for token in scope.active_registration_tokens:
            token.token

    provides:
        UserSetsActionsSecret(manager, scope, name, value) when scope.kind != instance
        UserDeletesActionsSecret(manager, secret)
        UserCreatesActionsVariable(manager, scope, name, value)
        UserUpdatesActionsVariable(manager, variable, name, value)
        UserDeletesActionsVariable(manager, variable)
        UserCreatesRunnerInScope(manager, scope, name, description, is_ephemeral)
        UserEditsRunnerDetails(manager, runner, name, description)
        UserRegeneratesRunnerSecret(manager, runner)
        UserDeletesRunnerFromScope(manager, runner)
        UserRequestsNewRegistrationToken(manager, scope)

    @guarantee SecretValuesNeverShown
        -- No interface ever returns a secret's value after it is set; it is
        -- only delivered to runners inside a task payload.

    @guidance
        -- may_manage_actions_scope: instance -> site admin; user -> that user
        -- (or a site admin via API); organization -> organization owner;
        -- repository -> repository admin (web) / owner (API).
        -- inherited_runners lists runners of wider scopes (instance, owner)
        -- that can serve this scope, read-only; only runners of exactly this
        -- scope are editable or deletable. A runner's task history is listed
        -- on its detail page.
}

-- The runner protocol (connect-RPC under /api/actions).
-- from: routers/api/actions/runner/runner.go:40
surface RunnerService {
    facing runner: RegisteredRunner
    context task: Task where runner = runner

    exposes:
        task.job.run.repository
        task.job.run.commit_sha
        task.job.run.ref
        task.job.run.event
        task.job.key
        task.job.runs_on
        task.token
        task_secrets(task)
        task_variables(task)
        needs_outputs(task)

    provides:
        RunnerDeclares(runner, labels, version)
        RunnerFetchesTask(runner, job, request_key)
        RunnerRetriesFetch(runner, request_key)
        RunnerReportsTaskProgress(runner, task) when task.status = running
        RunnerReportsTaskResult(runner, task, result) when task.status = running
        RunnerReportsTaskOutput(runner, task, key, value)
        RunnerAppendsTaskLog(runner, task, from_index, row_count, byte_count, no_more)
            when not task.log_archived
        RunnerSubmitsStepSummary(runner, step, content)

    contracts:
        fulfils RunnerProtocol

    @guarantee SecretsWithheldFromForks
        -- task_secrets is empty for runs from fork pull requests unless the
        -- trigger is pull_request_target; FORGEJO_TOKEN is always present.
        -- Inner jobs of a reusable workflow get the caller's secrets when
        -- `secrets: inherit`, else only those the caller maps explicitly.

    @guidance
        -- task_variables: instance, then owner, then repository variables,
        -- later ones overriding earlier ones (repository wins).
        -- task_secrets: owner secrets overridden by repository secrets.
}

-- Registration for a runner holding a registration token.
-- from: routers/api/actions/runner/runner.go:47
surface RunnerRegistration {
    facing agent: UnregisteredRunnerAgent

    provides:
        RunnerRegistersWithToken(agent, name, labels, version, is_ephemeral)
}

-- What a running job can do with its own credentials: the automatic token
-- (as FORGEJO_TOKEN against the API, git and LFS) and the runtime token
-- (artifacts, ID tokens).
-- API: GET /api/v1/actions/run (the run of the presenting token),
--      /api/actions_pipeline/... (artifacts v1-3), /twirp/github.actions.results.api.v1.ArtifactService/* (v4),
--      GET /api/actions/_apis/pipelines/workflows/{run}/idtoken?audience=,
--      /api/actions/.well-known/openid-configuration, /api/actions/keys
-- from: models/perm/access/repo_permission.go:143
surface RunningJobCapabilities {
    facing job_token: RunningJob
    context task: Task where status = running

    exposes:
        task.job.run.index
        task.job.run.status
        task.token_repository_access
        task.runtime_token_cache_scope
        task.oidc_enabled
        for artifact in task.job.run.artifacts:
            artifact.name when artifact.status = upload_confirmed
            artifact.size when artifact.status = upload_confirmed

    provides:
        TaskCreatesArtifact(job_token, name)
        TaskCreatesArtifactWithRetention(job_token, name, retention)
        TaskFinalizesArtifact(job_token, artifact, size)
        TaskRequestsIdToken(job_token, audience) when job_token.oidc_enabled

    contracts:
        fulfils ArtifactProtocol

    @guarantee AutomaticTokenScope
        -- On its own repository the automatic token acts as the Actions bot
        -- with write access to every enabled unit, or read access for fork
        -- pull-request runs (including pull_request_target). On any other
        -- repository it has only what the Actions bot has (public read).
        -- It stops working the moment the task stops running.
        -- Pushes made with it do not start workflows.

    @guidance
        -- The workflow `permissions:` key is not honoured; a run warns about it.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred WorkflowRun.job_definitions    -- see: code.forgejo.org/forgejo/runner act/jobparser (YAML, matrix, reusable workflows)
deferred Workflow.matching_workflows    -- see: modules/actions/workflows.go detectMatched (event/filter matching)
deferred ScheduleSpec.next_cron_occurrence  -- see: github.com/gdgvda/cron (5-field cron, @descriptors, TZ=/CRON_TZ= prefixes)

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Dispatching a disabled workflow is allowed by Forgejo (manual and API dispatch do not check the disabled list) while re-runs and scheduled runs of it are refused. Should dispatch also be refused?"
open question "Repository-scoped secrets/variables/runners need repository admin on the web UI but repository owner on the REST API. Which permission does the rebuild want?"
open question "Artifact retention requested by a job is not capped by ARTIFACT_RETENTION_DAYS. Should the instance setting be a maximum as well as the default?"
open question "The registration token is reusable until rotated and never expires. Should registration tokens expire or be single-use?"
open question "Should the legacy OIDC subject format (legacy_forgejo_15) be offered at all in the rebuild, or only the standard one?"
open question "Should the v1-v3 artifact protocol (still used by actions/upload-artifact@v3) be supported, or only v4?"
open question "Deleting a run discards its artifacts and logs; there is no retention for run records themselves. Should old runs be pruned automatically?"
open question "Scheduled workflows are never disabled for inactivity (GitHub disables after 60 days without repository activity). Keep Forgejo's behaviour?"

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------
-- REQUEST code/Push.ref_updates with RefUpdate.ref_kind/ref_name/new_sha (present); a black-box full_ref_name(update) / qualified_ref(kind, name) gives refs/heads/<b> or refs/tags/<t>.
-- REQUEST code: accept code/CommitStatusReported from the Actions bot (creator = actions_bot()) for the job's own repository without a write-permission check; target URL = the job page. Scheduled runs report no statuses (Forgejo skips them on runner updates).
-- REQUEST accounts: a well-known system user "the Actions bot" (actions_bot(), is_actions_bot(user)); events caused by it start no workflows.
-- REQUEST repositories/Repository.default_branch, .is_empty, .is_archived, .owner_user, .owner_org — used for scoping and gating.
-- REQUEST repositories: the actions unit's per-repository settings (disabled workflow file names, OIDC subject format) are modelled here as Workflow.is_disabled; repositories may prefer to own them on RepoUnit. actions_unit_enabled(repository) = the actions RepoUnit is enabled and actions is not in DISABLED_REPO_UNITS.
-- REQUEST access: can_read(user, repo, actions), can_write(user, repo, actions), is_repo_admin(user, repo). This module uses local black-box aliases can_read_actions / can_write_actions / is_repo_admin because qualified black-box calls cannot be stipulated in journeys; integration may substitute the access functions.
-- REQUEST access: the automatic token as an authentication method (TaskAccessesOwnRepository / TaskReadsOtherPublicRepository already model it) — note Forgejo grants write to every unit of the own repository, read for fork PR runs.
-- REQUEST issues: Issue.pull_request, Issue.milestone, Comment.issue (used to route issue vs pull-request activity).
-- REQUEST pulls/PullRequest.is_fork (head repository differs from base), .head_commit_sha (present), pull_ref(pr) = refs/pull/<index>/head, merge_commit_of(pr) = merged_commit_sha.
-- REQUEST releases/Release.publisher, .tag_name, .repository.
-- REQUEST packages/PackageVersion.package.repository (optional link).
-- REQUEST quota: quota_allows_artifacts(repository) = the repository owner's quota allows the artifacts subject; Artifact.compressed_size is provided for QuotaUsage.
-- REQUEST notifications: react to WorkflowJobCompleted(job, prior) — when the job failed and job.run.notify_email, mail the trigger user (repository owner for system-triggered runs) unless they disabled email notifications.
-- REQUEST webhooks: also react to WorkflowRunCompleted / WorkflowJobCompleted / WorkflowRunAttemptStarted / WorkflowJobAttemptStarted (this module splits final transitions out of *StatusChanged).
-- REQUEST administration: cron tasks stop_zombie_tasks (5m), stop_endless_tasks (30m), cancel_abandoned_jobs (6h), transfer_lingering_logs (midnight), start_schedule_tasks (1m), cleanup_actions (midnight), cleanup_offline_runners (disabled by default), actions_action_user (weekly); none registered when actions are disabled. Admin web pages /-/admin/actions/{runners,variables} map to ActionsSettings with the instance scope.
